1
00:00:04,850 --> 00:02:09,270
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:09,949 --> 00:02:12,270
Episode 86

3
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:18,920
We slept in the enemy's bosom.

4
00:02:19,290 --> 00:02:21,500
Just beside them.

5
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,620
We took place in their hearts.

6
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:35,250
We learned
their minds, souls, trades, faiths.1

7
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,490
We captured them.

8
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:45,160
It's time to awaken the ones
who sleep under the false light.

9
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:49,380
Now is time to wake up.

10
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:53,520
They took roots to these lands.

11
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:59,710
We'll break their branches and
root them up.

12
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:07,680
Every mob that finds swords...

13
00:03:07,890 --> 00:03:09,960
can turn into an army.

14
00:03:10,170 --> 00:03:15,060
But preparing a commander takes
decades.

15
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,160
Whatever they have among them...

16
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:25,250
intellectuals, scholars...

17
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:27,880
elders, commanders...

18
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:30,790
we'll destroy them all.

19
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,960
Wake up!

20
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:45,820
You are the ones who awakened
the first.

21
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:47,960
The ones who woke up to destroy.

22
00:03:57,360 --> 00:04:02,420
You are more dangerous than this
poison in my hand.

23
00:04:14,370 --> 00:04:16,959
According to Mari, a girl
with no one.

24
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:23,360
According to Turks, a helpless girl
serving Mari.

25
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:28,840
But our most capable killer.

26
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:34,800
I'll destroy their union...

27
00:04:35,410 --> 00:04:39,760
from inside, right from the center.

28
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:44,970
Their commander showed
their weakness.

29
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:48,800
Let their weakness bring their
end, Cornellia.

30
00:04:49,940 --> 00:04:56,520
If their best commanders Turgut
and Gündüz are getting on bad terms.

31
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,500
This will turn bloody.

32
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:14,330
Whose end will be caused
by this poison, sir?

33
00:05:15,150 --> 00:05:19,550
Mari, who you've been living
with for years.

34
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:29,590
I buried my father.

35
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:31,940
My heart is burning, Osman.

36
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:36,170
He died before seeing
his grandson.

37
00:05:42,420 --> 00:05:44,110
Umur Bey is a martyr.

38
00:05:46,810 --> 00:05:48,900
We are witnesses to that.

39
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:52,040
You should be my witness that...

40
00:05:52,630 --> 00:05:54,960
I'll take the lives of who
did this to him.

41
00:05:55,830 --> 00:05:57,900
I don't doubt that at all, Osman.

42
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:00,760
My father's blood won't be forgotten.

43
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:02,270
I know it.

44
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:13,290
You are a strong woman.

45
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:16,490
You will overcome this too.

46
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:20,200
And I'll always be with you.

47
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:30,060
But if you allow me now...

48
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:34,130
I need to talk to Sultan Mesud now.

49
00:06:34,930 --> 00:06:36,260
Yes, Osman.

50
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:04,540
You buried your dead.

51
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:09,690
Now, it's time to give answers, Osman!

52
00:07:09,910 --> 00:07:11,160
My sultan.

53
00:07:18,010 --> 00:07:21,990
There isn't a single move that I can't
answer for, my sultan.

54
00:07:26,450 --> 00:07:28,940
What do you want me to answer?

55
00:07:28,980 --> 00:07:33,990
You killed the vizier of the Seljuks
in front of my eyes!

56
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:37,690
You couldn't do it to me so
you did to him!

57
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:42,040
I won't waste breath to say
what you did.

58
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:46,320
The only words that will come
out of my mouth will be...

59
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,500
your death sentence.

60
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,220
My sultan.

61
00:07:54,970 --> 00:07:58,050
Your decision is unjust.

62
00:08:01,650 --> 00:08:04,780
If Vizier Alemşah was alive now...

63
00:08:06,090 --> 00:08:08,440
he would tell everything.

64
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:12,980
But...

65
00:08:14,510 --> 00:08:17,020
but his time was over.

66
00:08:20,170 --> 00:08:21,910
If the heads don't speak...

67
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:27,250
then others will.

68
00:09:00,530 --> 00:09:01,910
My sultan.

69
00:09:02,770 --> 00:09:05,110
I'm your subject, a Seljuk commander,
Konur.

70
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:17,290
They will speak now, my sultan.

71
00:09:19,150 --> 00:09:24,080
I considered my service to Vizier Alemşah
as serving you, my sultan.

72
00:09:25,550 --> 00:09:27,240
I beg your forgiveness.

73
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:32,080
Stop gabbling and
speak the truth.

74
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,450
My sultan.

75
00:09:37,550 --> 00:09:41,880
Vizier Alemşah have done many
tyranny with your name.

76
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:45,450
Even the ones I personally
witnessed...

77
00:09:46,090 --> 00:09:48,440
are making it sure that
he deserves to be killed.

78
00:09:48,490 --> 00:09:51,250
Who is holding the strings of the vizier?

79
00:09:57,340 --> 00:09:58,920
My sultan.

80
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:02,420
Vizier Alemşah...

81
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,640
attempted to kill Osman Bey.

82
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,130
Isn't this what a rebel...

83
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:11,220
who tries to kill me deserves?

84
00:10:38,210 --> 00:10:39,670
Tell me, Barkın.

85
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:43,250
Where and how did this happen?
Everything.

86
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:45,300
I wish I didn't go ahead.

87
00:10:46,690 --> 00:10:48,580
I wish I didn't leave my uncle alone.

88
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:54,220
I wish we had died together.

89
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:56,280
Not you, Selvi.

90
00:10:57,620 --> 00:11:00,040
I should've been under the ground.

91
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:03,820
I'm too ashamed to hold
my head straight.

92
00:11:07,650 --> 00:11:10,210
End my shame, Malhun Hatun.

93
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:15,720
I couldn't protect, Umur Bey.

94
00:11:17,140 --> 00:11:18,920
I'm afraid of my Allah.

95
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,560
I can't take my life.

96
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:23,720
Save me from this burden.

97
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:25,180
Enough!

98
00:11:27,650 --> 00:11:30,340
I need the ones who killed my father,
Barkın.

99
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:34,180
Stop crying now and tell me
what happened!

100
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:38,400
Mongols.

101
00:11:39,350 --> 00:11:40,860
Mongols did it

102
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:43,800
Who was the commander?

103
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:45,260
How many were they?

104
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:47,080
They were many.

105
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:49,920
I couldn't see it.

106
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:55,520
Neither Umur Bey nor I had any alps
survive.

107
00:11:58,110 --> 00:12:04,030
In front of my eyes, they slaughtered
all my valiants.

108
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:08,320
When I was fighting with two Mongols...

109
00:12:08,940 --> 00:12:10,560
I fell wounded.

110
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:12,660
When I was closing my eyes...

111
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,560
I saw Umur Bey fell too.

112
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,730
Give him some time, Malhun.

113
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,120
Don't you see how Barkın is?

114
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:33,720
He loved my uncle too.

115
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:37,600
They killed him in front of
his eyes.

116
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,620
He is worse than us now.

117
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:43,350
I buried my father.

118
00:12:47,490 --> 00:12:50,990
The ones who killed him won't
even have graves.

119
00:13:00,990 --> 00:13:03,320
I didn't come here to listen to tales,
Osman.

120
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:08,270
I know what I've seen.
You stabbed me on my back!

121
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:10,380
It's not a tale, my sultan.

122
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:13,810
Mingiyan will tell everything.

123
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,180
Speak.

124
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:23,020
How did you attack me?

125
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:28,140
Tell him how your grand plan was.

126
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:33,870
Tell the co-operation of
Geyhatu and the vizier.

127
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:45,680
Tell how that dagger ended up
on the sultan's back.

128
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:51,060
Speak.

129
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:57,980
Alemşah informed us when Osman
got captured.

130
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:05,330
We gave his dagger to your
helper.

131
00:14:08,040 --> 00:14:10,600
Your helper Selman is loyal...

132
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:13,400
to great Geyhatu.

133
00:14:16,410 --> 00:14:23,160
We were going to get rid of
Osman and you.

134
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:27,630
But Osman...

135
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:30,980
This won't clean your name, Osman.

136
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:37,620
They speak as you want to not
end up like the vizier.

137
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:40,630
My verdict is clear.

138
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:45,240
Let's say it's true.

139
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:48,440
What about the other truth?

140
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:54,360
Why did you agree with Emperor Andrenikos?

141
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:55,950
My sultan.

142
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:00,930
If you ask me about
my deal with the emperor...

143
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:06,240
the lord should answer that.

144
00:15:09,690 --> 00:15:11,020
Boran.

145
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:21,490
Sultan, his grace.

146
00:15:23,410 --> 00:15:24,740
Osman Bey.

147
00:15:26,850 --> 00:15:28,640
I'm Aya Nikola.

148
00:15:29,050 --> 00:15:33,200
I came here today to speak
the truth only.

149
00:15:34,130 --> 00:15:37,860
I took Osman to the emperor
personally.

150
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:47,003
After all, he wanted us on his side
against Geyhatu and the Mongols.

151
00:15:47,156 --> 00:15:49,220
It's just that.

152
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:54,400
You speak, Michael Kosses.

153
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:57,060
Sultan Mesud, your grace.

154
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,580
I've known Osman Bey for years.

155
00:16:00,910 --> 00:16:05,560
We have fought together on the
battlefield many times.

156
00:16:06,330 --> 00:16:10,660
I'm convinced that Osman Bey's
only goal...

157
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:14,670
is to protect these lands and
sustain peace and stability.

158
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:21,540
Everyone here knows the Vizier and
Geyhatu's intentions clearly.

159
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:27,680
Their goal is to destroy you, us,
everyone.

160
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:32,060
For this reason, they came with
flying fire.

161
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:36,910
Everyone, out.

162
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:04,118
What you say, what you show,
your witnesses...

163
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:11,720
I'm finally convinced, Osman Bey.

164
00:17:18,310 --> 00:17:19,730
The dead deserved death.

165
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:25,160
But I can't let you kill Geyhatu.

166
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:29,110
Geyhatu is my captive, my sultan.

167
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:35,790
His death or survival...

168
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:40,430
is my decision.

169
00:17:45,870 --> 00:17:48,390
If Geyhatu won't die...

170
00:17:53,370 --> 00:17:55,470
then I get my right.

171
00:17:56,540 --> 00:18:01,080
If you kill Geyhatu, Argun will
raze our lands.

172
00:18:01,250 --> 00:18:03,110
He'll kill us all, Osman!

173
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:07,430
Is there anything better
than saving our lands?

174
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:08,870
My sultan.

175
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:17,030
Ever since my grandfather Süleyman Shah,
my father Ertuğrul Ghazi, we fight.

176
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:21,940
We were destroyed tens of times.

177
00:18:23,410 --> 00:18:25,790
We died thousands of times.

178
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:30,120
We aren't afraid at all.

179
00:18:31,630 --> 00:18:32,970
But...

180
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:36,920
if Geyhatu will live...

181
00:18:38,210 --> 00:18:44,730
in return, I want the villages in
Yenişehir borders.

182
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:51,480
I want weapons for my alps to equip.

183
00:18:53,260 --> 00:18:55,530
I want horses for a campaign.

184
00:18:57,750 --> 00:19:00,220
And to hit those tyrants...

185
00:19:01,570 --> 00:19:03,320
I want bows.

186
00:19:05,950 --> 00:19:08,340
This jihad is our breath.

187
00:19:09,340 --> 00:19:12,440
A nation not fighting to advance...

188
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:15,450
will lose its liberty first.

189
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:25,350
The existence of the Turks can only be
possible with conquest.

190
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:33,810
You always ride your horse forward.

191
00:19:36,670 --> 00:19:40,370
You'll receive what you want, Osman Bey.

192
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:08,140
Cornelia!

193
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,490
I've been looking for you
all day. Where are you?

194
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:15,600
You wanted a pie last night.

195
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:17,680
So I went to get one.

196
00:20:35,070 --> 00:20:37,400
My lady, are you alright?

197
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:41,250
Mari!

198
00:20:46,090 --> 00:20:48,280
What's wrong?
Are you alright?

199
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:51,050
My nausea doesn't leave me.

200
00:20:52,250 --> 00:20:55,060
It will leave in time.

201
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:57,630
Go to your tent and
get some rest.

202
00:20:57,880 --> 00:20:58,880
Cornelia.

203
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,830
Come with me. Let's prepare
some meals.

204
00:21:02,070 --> 00:21:03,430
Alright.

205
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:09,420
Mari.

206
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:14,660
Turgut Bey!

207
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:20,300
Tell me, Barkın.

208
00:21:22,050 --> 00:21:23,570
Turgut Bey.

209
00:21:24,860 --> 00:21:26,410
I admire you.

210
00:21:28,820 --> 00:21:31,910
If someone has given my wife
to the enemy...

211
00:21:35,820 --> 00:21:37,620
I would kill him.

212
00:21:40,950 --> 00:21:42,470
Barkın.

213
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:46,570
If it was up to me, I would've
kiled him long ago.

214
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:49,460
He should be thankful for Osman Bey.

215
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:53,440
You are right.

216
00:21:53,590 --> 00:21:55,630
You are right but...

217
00:21:56,510 --> 00:21:57,880
one who does it once...

218
00:21:59,180 --> 00:22:01,700
can do it again, Turgut Bey.

219
00:22:03,150 --> 00:22:05,220
How can Osman Bey trust Gündüz?

220
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:08,420
I couldn't believe what I heard.

221
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,540
I tyrannized the women here.

222
00:22:18,550 --> 00:22:19,880
It's true.

223
00:22:22,820 --> 00:22:24,850
I understand everything.

224
00:22:25,130 --> 00:22:27,720
Taking Orhan away from
his mother?

225
00:22:28,700 --> 00:22:31,040
The one who does this to
a little child...

226
00:22:32,420 --> 00:22:34,120
can do anything.

227
00:22:41,190 --> 00:22:43,480
But Osman Bey made his decision.

228
00:22:43,860 --> 00:22:45,950
It's not up to us to speak.

229
00:23:05,460 --> 00:23:08,090
Sultan Mesud saved your life.

230
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:14,920
But not only your feet, even your horse
won't touch these lands again.

231
00:23:20,860 --> 00:23:22,070
Get up.

232
00:23:30,610 --> 00:23:36,140
I'm not Alemşah.
You can't kill me.

233
00:23:38,170 --> 00:23:44,270
I'll come with an army.
I will destroy your tribe.

234
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:49,740
I'll rip your and your children's hearts!

235
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:51,060
Don't!

236
00:23:51,110 --> 00:23:52,400
Don't!

237
00:23:52,420 --> 00:23:53,780
Don't!

238
00:23:53,980 --> 00:23:56,560
I'll make this tent your grave.

239
00:23:56,580 --> 00:24:00,640
You killed my alps.

240
00:24:03,100 --> 00:24:04,310
You...

241
00:24:05,540 --> 00:24:07,560
burned my heart!

242
00:24:10,590 --> 00:24:12,660
You made brothers kill
each other!

243
00:24:21,660 --> 00:24:24,860
I will do much worse!

244
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:29,600
When Argun hears what you
did to me...

245
00:24:29,940 --> 00:24:33,780
he'll move to slay you.

246
00:24:34,600 --> 00:24:41,720
You should be afraid of what
Argun Khan will hear, not me.

247
00:24:45,900 --> 00:24:47,900
Speak clearly, Osman.

248
00:24:49,020 --> 00:24:51,800
Your treachery isn't only against
Islam...

249
00:24:52,330 --> 00:24:54,360
not only Turks...

250
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:58,490
you betrayed much more people.

251
00:25:01,470 --> 00:25:04,590
You won't die that easily.

252
00:25:08,030 --> 00:25:09,880
You will die as you lived.

253
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:20,630
What did you do, Osman?

254
00:25:21,410 --> 00:25:23,320
You will see that soon.

255
00:25:27,210 --> 00:25:29,400
What did you do, Osman?

256
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:31,830
Osman!

257
00:26:24,340 --> 00:26:26,660
Your dogs killed my father.

258
00:26:27,370 --> 00:26:30,320
I'll leave your corpse
on here, Geyhatu.

259
00:26:33,740 --> 00:26:35,800
Die, rat!

260
00:26:39,950 --> 00:26:41,450
Malhun!

261
00:26:43,590 --> 00:26:45,830
Long live Osman Bey!

262
00:26:51,570 --> 00:26:54,640
You can't release him from here
with my father's blood on his hands.

263
00:27:03,850 --> 00:27:05,560
It's not Osman's order.

264
00:27:07,070 --> 00:27:09,740
It's the ruler's order.

265
00:27:11,120 --> 00:27:12,680
Stay back, woman.

266
00:27:13,300 --> 00:27:14,660
It's not just.

267
00:27:14,720 --> 00:27:17,260
You can't release this tyrant!

268
00:27:18,920 --> 00:27:20,260
Malhun!

269
00:27:20,340 --> 00:27:21,390
Osman!

270
00:27:32,060 --> 00:27:33,380
Malhun.

271
00:27:54,100 --> 00:27:55,400
Malhun.

272
00:27:55,410 --> 00:27:59,280
I've never seen any action fueled
by anger end well.

273
00:27:59,660 --> 00:28:02,160
He is leaving with my father's blood.

274
00:28:09,750 --> 00:28:11,140
Traitor!

275
00:28:19,630 --> 00:28:22,180
May his destination be grave.

276
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:26,180
It will be, mother.

277
00:28:26,740 --> 00:28:28,100
It will be.

278
00:28:34,060 --> 00:28:37,340
He leaves the revenge
of his tribe.

279
00:28:37,780 --> 00:28:40,480
What kind of loyalty is this?

280
00:28:42,360 --> 00:28:45,580
I'll take it all.

281
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:52,840
Long live Osman Bey!

282
00:28:52,950 --> 00:28:56,120
Long live Osman Bey!

283
00:29:28,330 --> 00:29:30,840
Don't make another mistake, Osman Bey.

284
00:29:54,410 --> 00:29:56,640
I got what I want, my sultan.

285
00:30:02,660 --> 00:30:04,860
I took his teeth.

286
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:11,200
He can't come to these lands again.

287
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:21,780
Untie commander Geyhatu.

288
00:30:57,410 --> 00:30:58,930
Mingiyan!

289
00:31:11,550 --> 00:31:13,510
Your tongue will be knot...

290
00:31:14,200 --> 00:31:18,260
no knife be able to
unknot it.

291
00:31:18,360 --> 00:31:21,360
If you speak, you are dead, Mingiyan.

292
00:31:30,310 --> 00:31:32,340
If someone is dying...

293
00:31:33,900 --> 00:31:35,960
it's me who is swinging
the sword.

294
00:31:47,840 --> 00:31:49,500
Now get out of my face.

295
00:32:11,240 --> 00:32:15,500
Osman is growing stronger.

296
00:32:16,720 --> 00:32:19,500
But our enemy is taken away
as a captive.

297
00:32:19,550 --> 00:32:25,660
An enemy more dangerous than ever
is borning, Kosses.

298
00:32:25,660 --> 00:32:28,270
More than ever.

299
00:32:36,140 --> 00:32:37,620
Kayı people!

300
00:32:39,550 --> 00:32:44,220
The slanders on Osman Bey is
cleared away.

301
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:50,250
He is innocent of all his accusations.

302
00:32:57,440 --> 00:33:02,410
I, Seljuk ruler, Sultan Mesud...

303
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:07,790
gave Osman Bey the lands he wanted.

304
00:33:14,540 --> 00:33:21,320
The villages on Yenişehir borders
belong to Osman Bey now.

305
00:33:21,320 --> 00:33:45,370
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

306
00:33:49,810 --> 00:33:54,980
Now, your lands expanded with
your new lands.

307
00:33:57,090 --> 00:33:59,220
The borders are under your protection.

308
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:04,440
Soon, I'll send you troops.

309
00:34:05,380 --> 00:34:08,590
The lands you give will be
our frontiers for new conquests.

310
00:34:09,050 --> 00:34:13,580
The troops you send will
fight for Islam.

311
00:34:15,530 --> 00:34:20,340
We all will struggle for
the world's order.

312
00:34:22,050 --> 00:34:23,620
Be at ease.

313
00:34:26,389 --> 00:34:28,500
We will be victorious.

314
00:34:36,300 --> 00:34:38,000
Godspeed.

315
00:35:27,680 --> 00:35:29,040
Boran.

316
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:31,640
My bey.

317
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:34,630
Inform the alps and the beys.

318
00:35:35,400 --> 00:35:37,420
Call them to my tent this evening.

319
00:35:40,600 --> 00:35:42,620
It's time for conquest now.

320
00:35:42,670 --> 00:35:44,230
As you order, my bey.

321
00:35:51,640 --> 00:35:55,680
The alps need a valiant such
as you.

322
00:35:57,100 --> 00:36:00,610
Why would a stranger like
Turgut be the Head alp?

323
00:36:06,630 --> 00:36:09,770
Turgut is an independent man.

324
00:36:10,760 --> 00:36:15,180
What did he control so far
that he can control the alps?

325
00:36:16,650 --> 00:36:19,510
You couldn't protect Umur Bey, Barkın Bey.

326
00:36:20,300 --> 00:36:22,050
What are you talking about here?

327
00:36:22,770 --> 00:36:24,490
Go and mind your own business.

328
00:36:36,340 --> 00:36:38,680
Söğüt

329
00:36:39,210 --> 00:36:42,870
Osman Bey is coming tomorrow.
I don't want problems.

330
00:36:43,510 --> 00:36:46,890
Prepare everything.

331
00:36:46,890 --> 00:36:50,050
Don't worry, Akça Dervish.
We won't shame you.

332
00:36:50,050 --> 00:36:51,350
Thank you.

333
00:36:57,890 --> 00:36:59,450
Salam Alaikum.

334
00:36:59,450 --> 00:37:03,210
Alaikum Salam.

335
00:37:05,140 --> 00:37:06,680
You look like a traveler.

336
00:37:07,180 --> 00:37:10,980
We are all travelers on the road of
The Middle Way.

337
00:37:10,980 --> 00:37:12,980
We want to reach Allah.

338
00:37:14,180 --> 00:37:15,940
This is the first time I see you.

339
00:37:16,060 --> 00:37:18,610
Where are you coming from?
Where are you going to?

340
00:37:18,700 --> 00:37:21,240
We are coming from Semerkant
with my student.

341
00:37:21,810 --> 00:37:26,000
We travel for our faith
and stay at public houses.

342
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:28,520
They call me İbrahim Fakih.

343
00:37:30,590 --> 00:37:32,620
You are most welcome here.

344
00:37:32,620 --> 00:37:33,980
Thank you.

345
00:37:34,550 --> 00:37:36,390
Let's get you to your room.

346
00:37:36,390 --> 00:37:39,300
-You should get some rest.
-On the contrary.

347
00:37:39,550 --> 00:37:44,350
I've been sleeping for a long time.
I'm energetic and ready for the mission.

348
00:37:45,510 --> 00:37:47,500
When our mission is Allah's path...

349
00:37:47,870 --> 00:37:50,120
You are in the right place,
İbrahim Efendi.

350
00:37:50,750 --> 00:37:53,600
I know. I know, brother.

351
00:37:53,600 --> 00:37:57,630
I've been hearing Söğüt's
unbreakable unity.

352
00:38:18,110 --> 00:38:19,890
You came before me, huh?

353
00:38:25,990 --> 00:38:27,410
I'm at your service.

354
00:38:30,780 --> 00:38:32,550
I poisoned Gündüz and Turgut.

355
00:38:33,650 --> 00:38:35,640
The daggers will shine soon.

356
00:38:37,510 --> 00:38:40,620
That poison will start a fire, Barkın.

357
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:45,300
It'll start with a tent...

358
00:38:47,630 --> 00:38:50,130
then it will spread...

359
00:38:51,220 --> 00:38:55,050
spread, spread...

360
00:38:56,180 --> 00:39:01,730
that fire will burn Söğüt.

361
00:39:04,290 --> 00:39:06,260
We've awaken.

362
00:39:07,200 --> 00:39:10,190
They'll sleep forever.

363
00:39:14,110 --> 00:39:17,360
Umur's death has shaken them.

364
00:39:19,240 --> 00:39:22,670
We are sowing doubt on their minds.

365
00:39:24,120 --> 00:39:26,990
The fear inside them will
turn into anger.

366
00:39:27,910 --> 00:39:31,940
This fear is the fear of darkness, Barkın.

367
00:39:32,380 --> 00:39:34,680
They can't see their enemies.

368
00:39:36,880 --> 00:39:39,250
Kayı Tribe will surrender.

369
00:39:40,130 --> 00:39:41,940
Who'll set the fire?

370
00:39:44,820 --> 00:39:48,520
Mari's loyal servant Cornelia.

371
00:39:49,170 --> 00:39:53,230
She'll start the war by killing
a beloved one.

372
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:59,050
What will I do?

373
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:10,430
With the name of Allah.

374
00:40:11,940 --> 00:40:14,760
How can she not eat all day?

375
00:40:15,720 --> 00:40:19,110
Mari needs to be careful with
this.

376
00:40:19,110 --> 00:40:22,450
You are right, Ayşe Hatun.
She is pregnant now.

377
00:40:22,450 --> 00:40:24,490
She should think for her child.

378
00:40:24,490 --> 00:40:25,850
Yes.

379
00:40:30,740 --> 00:40:33,550
I won't feel good. I should
prepare a salver for her.

380
00:40:33,550 --> 00:40:34,900
Alright.

381
00:40:40,080 --> 00:40:42,350
She'll be a great mother.

382
00:40:46,340 --> 00:40:49,390
She will. Wouldn't she?

383
00:40:49,390 --> 00:40:52,320
She is pretty, her baby is pretty.

384
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:09,473
With the name of Allah.

385
00:41:10,220 --> 00:41:12,480
Put it here.

386
00:41:13,200 --> 00:41:14,780
Enjoy it.

387
00:41:14,910 --> 00:41:18,040
-Make sure that she eats it all.
-Alright.

388
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:34,610
We'll fight without disguises,
without hiding.

389
00:41:37,330 --> 00:41:39,200
Inshallah, brother.

390
00:41:40,490 --> 00:41:45,730
From now, we should be open and not
repeat the old issues.

391
00:41:46,230 --> 00:41:51,100
Otherwise, there are people who hide
better than you and work with the tyrants.

392
00:41:52,520 --> 00:41:56,050
Is there anyone more tyrant than one
who steps over the fallen?

393
00:41:57,510 --> 00:42:01,380
Don't get arrogant with your position
and choose wrong words, Turgut Bey.

394
00:42:01,420 --> 00:42:04,080
-Gündüz Bey, don't--
-Turgut Bey.

395
00:42:22,430 --> 00:42:25,250
Now, we are saved from two troubles.

396
00:42:27,420 --> 00:42:30,650
Just like arrows flying out of my bow.

397
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:36,860
Now, we'll march to the enemy.

398
00:42:52,320 --> 00:42:57,610
Our target is İnegöl.

399
00:42:59,570 --> 00:43:00,880
My bey.

400
00:43:01,500 --> 00:43:06,800
When I see Nikola, anger flows
in my veins.

401
00:43:07,660 --> 00:43:12,290
We'll avenge our brothers.

402
00:43:12,810 --> 00:43:18,060
But our cause isn't a cause of revenge.

403
00:43:18,520 --> 00:43:23,230
Our cause is Allah's words.

404
00:43:23,770 --> 00:43:25,340
Thank Allah.

405
00:43:25,370 --> 00:43:26,940
Thank Allah.

406
00:43:27,090 --> 00:43:31,620
We know the interior of İnegöl very well.

407
00:43:31,970 --> 00:43:36,740
We know the weak points of it's walls.

408
00:43:38,540 --> 00:43:40,600
Master Akça.

409
00:43:41,600 --> 00:43:42,990
Say it.

410
00:43:43,820 --> 00:43:47,900
We hid the Greek Fire with Master Davut.

411
00:44:19,370 --> 00:44:20,670
My bey.

412
00:44:22,040 --> 00:44:25,370
There are two ways to take down
the walls.

413
00:44:26,900 --> 00:44:31,510
We'll fill the round shots with fire.

414
00:44:32,990 --> 00:44:37,290
They will stuck on the wall and explode.

415
00:44:38,820 --> 00:44:41,400
Or...

416
00:44:44,190 --> 00:44:50,600
capable alps will shoot them...

417
00:44:53,630 --> 00:44:55,140
with fire arrows.

418
00:45:06,220 --> 00:45:07,770
Master Davud.

419
00:45:07,830 --> 00:45:09,160
My bey.

420
00:45:09,160 --> 00:45:11,810
Where will we shoot, Master Davud?

421
00:45:12,040 --> 00:45:17,270
The stones on the west are strong,
hard to destruct.

422
00:45:17,830 --> 00:45:23,040
But the stones on the east are
weaker.

423
00:45:23,620 --> 00:45:26,920
If we open a hole between
two sides.

424
00:45:27,110 --> 00:45:32,090
We'll see the street leading
to Nikola's interior castle.

425
00:45:32,160 --> 00:45:37,540
When we reach Nikola and behead him,
the castle is ours.

426
00:45:39,130 --> 00:45:42,570
Do we have enough catapults?

427
00:45:44,600 --> 00:45:46,290
We don't, my bey.

428
00:45:47,050 --> 00:45:52,970
But if we wait for Sultan's help,
our catapults will be enough.

429
00:45:55,790 --> 00:45:59,210
We'll start the siege early.

430
00:45:59,940 --> 00:46:03,750
Sultan's help will join us if they come.

431
00:46:04,880 --> 00:46:08,400
But say it. Nikola must be on
guard now.

432
00:46:09,460 --> 00:46:13,830
Including the roads, everywhere
must be filled with traps.

433
00:46:14,730 --> 00:46:16,270
Now...

434
00:46:17,350 --> 00:46:23,270
How will we position these catapults...

435
00:46:23,310 --> 00:46:26,760
this near to the castle?

436
00:46:51,470 --> 00:46:54,500
It's delicious, Cornelia.

437
00:47:01,990 --> 00:47:04,260
Do you want some?

438
00:47:05,710 --> 00:47:10,240
I appreciate it, my lady.
You need to eat for your baby too.

439
00:47:18,540 --> 00:47:21,160
I wish to see you as a mother too.

440
00:47:23,530 --> 00:47:25,550
This feeling...

441
00:47:27,750 --> 00:47:29,990
motherhood...

442
00:47:31,110 --> 00:47:32,660
it's different.

443
00:47:40,060 --> 00:47:44,410
I should go and help the women now.

444
00:47:50,600 --> 00:47:52,410
Good night.

445
00:47:53,410 --> 00:47:55,240
Good night, my lady.

446
00:47:59,890 --> 00:48:05,140
We are awakened, my lady.
But you'll be sleeping forever.

447
00:48:11,110 --> 00:48:12,470
Master Akça.

448
00:48:13,880 --> 00:48:17,890
You are building the catapults.
You are the master.

449
00:48:18,480 --> 00:48:24,950
Now say it, how long does it take
to build it when you have all components?

450
00:48:27,240 --> 00:48:29,220
With all the components?

451
00:48:29,580 --> 00:48:31,010
All of them.

452
00:48:39,350 --> 00:48:41,230
Half a day.

453
00:48:42,560 --> 00:48:44,310
My bey.

454
00:48:44,480 --> 00:48:48,050
We should hide them in a caravan.

455
00:48:48,350 --> 00:48:53,320
When we get closer to the castle,
you know it, these woods are thick.

456
00:48:53,880 --> 00:48:56,490
They are close to the eastern side.

457
00:48:56,610 --> 00:49:00,490
If we build the catapults there...

458
00:49:00,790 --> 00:49:06,580
Nikola will see the flying fire in
the morning instead of the sun.

459
00:49:11,460 --> 00:49:13,080
Master Davud.

460
00:49:13,130 --> 00:49:14,240
My bey.

461
00:49:14,440 --> 00:49:18,090
Is what Gündüz Bey says possible?

462
00:49:19,350 --> 00:49:21,120
It's possible, my bey.

463
00:49:22,380 --> 00:49:23,810
But...

464
00:49:24,330 --> 00:49:27,860
a catapult that is made in the darkness
of the night...

465
00:49:27,970 --> 00:49:29,360
Is no good for anyone.

466
00:49:33,590 --> 00:49:36,880
It's half-moon. It'll be dark, Osman Bey.

467
00:49:37,470 --> 00:49:41,920
If we use torches, we'll reveal
ourselves to Nikola.

468
00:49:42,450 --> 00:49:45,130
It's not reasonable.

469
00:49:57,750 --> 00:50:00,020
It'll be as Gündüz Bey says.

470
00:50:02,730 --> 00:50:04,830
This is how we'll take İnegöl.

471
00:50:05,610 --> 00:50:09,900
But we'll take İğnehisar first.

472
00:50:10,570 --> 00:50:16,510
It'll be our quarters.
Then, we'll march to İnegöl.

473
00:50:20,285 --> 00:50:22,310
Make your preperations.

474
00:50:46,485 --> 00:50:48,045
Mari.

475
00:50:51,285 --> 00:50:52,865
Turgut.

476
00:50:56,665 --> 00:50:58,385
Are you alright?

477
00:50:58,805 --> 00:51:00,365
I'm alright.
I'm alright.

478
00:51:01,185 --> 00:51:02,565
I'm alright.

479
00:51:02,925 --> 00:51:04,445
Who are you mad at?

480
00:51:04,485 --> 00:51:05,845
Say it.

481
00:51:07,745 --> 00:51:09,825
How did you know?

482
00:51:12,185 --> 00:51:13,525
From here.

483
00:51:19,445 --> 00:51:23,805
Ever since I've known you,
you are in some trouble.

484
00:51:26,085 --> 00:51:28,965
One comes after the other.

485
00:51:30,025 --> 00:51:33,305
I've never seen you sleep in peace.

486
00:51:36,925 --> 00:51:38,245
True.

487
00:51:39,445 --> 00:51:41,325
Our life is harsh.

488
00:51:41,825 --> 00:51:44,065
But do you know how I stay patient?

489
00:51:47,745 --> 00:51:49,085
With you.

490
00:51:51,305 --> 00:51:53,725
I forget it when I see you.

491
00:51:54,825 --> 00:51:56,965
Maybe I don't sleep in peace but...

492
00:51:58,085 --> 00:51:59,825
when I close my eyes...

493
00:52:01,905 --> 00:52:03,685
I see us.

494
00:52:06,125 --> 00:52:08,145
Our growing child...

495
00:52:10,625 --> 00:52:12,945
and beautiful days to come.

496
00:52:18,745 --> 00:52:20,825
Our future...

497
00:52:22,865 --> 00:52:24,585
will be beautiful.

498
00:52:25,605 --> 00:52:27,305
It will be beautiful.

499
00:52:34,845 --> 00:52:36,915
Söğüt

500
00:52:38,065 --> 00:52:40,205
Welcome, Osman Bey.

501
00:52:40,650 --> 00:52:42,190
Allah bless you.

502
00:52:42,290 --> 00:52:44,290
Allah bless you.

503
00:52:44,290 --> 00:52:46,750
Welcome, Osman Bey.

504
00:52:46,750 --> 00:52:49,010
Thank you.
Thank you.

505
00:52:49,010 --> 00:52:52,050
Welcome, my bey!

506
00:52:52,050 --> 00:52:54,890
No need.

507
00:52:55,090 --> 00:52:56,570
How's business?

508
00:52:56,570 --> 00:52:59,110
Thank Allah. Thank Allah, my bey.

509
00:52:59,110 --> 00:53:00,550
-Thanks to you.
-Mashallah.

510
00:53:00,550 --> 00:53:01,850
Mashallah.

511
00:53:01,850 --> 00:53:03,850
Have a good day.

512
00:53:05,420 --> 00:53:07,160
Good day, Hasan the Honey Seller!

513
00:53:07,160 --> 00:53:08,860
Welcome, my bey.

514
00:53:09,050 --> 00:53:11,230
-Thank you.
-You too, my bey.

515
00:53:11,230 --> 00:53:13,230
Let us taste your honey.

516
00:53:13,230 --> 00:53:15,790
It's the same with
the last one. Here.

517
00:53:18,550 --> 00:53:19,910
With Allah's name.

518
00:53:19,950 --> 00:53:21,450
Enjoy it, my bey.

519
00:53:25,530 --> 00:53:27,230
Weigh this again.

520
00:53:30,030 --> 00:53:31,730
Why should I weigh it again?

521
00:53:32,630 --> 00:53:37,070
It's not fair that you ask the same
price for crushed apples.

522
00:53:37,770 --> 00:53:40,470
Either put a different price
for the crushed ones...

523
00:53:40,470 --> 00:53:43,290
and I'll pay separately...

524
00:53:43,290 --> 00:53:45,290
or weigh the healthy ones only...

525
00:53:45,410 --> 00:53:46,970
and I'll buy them.

526
00:53:50,210 --> 00:53:53,770
Is this just for these two apples?

527
00:53:56,630 --> 00:53:58,010
Look.

528
00:54:02,490 --> 00:54:06,940
If I grant you this, there will be no
punishment for you in the afterlife.

529
00:54:07,590 --> 00:54:10,970
Take it if you want.
I won't feel its loss.

530
00:54:10,970 --> 00:54:19,530
But you adding haram to your profit
for two apples makes me feel bad.

531
00:54:20,270 --> 00:54:23,190
The haram you eat is so bad that...

532
00:54:23,970 --> 00:54:26,470
only the flames of hell can
cleanse it.

533
00:54:30,490 --> 00:54:32,270
You are right.

534
00:54:32,850 --> 00:54:34,390
I apologize.

535
00:54:34,910 --> 00:54:36,430
Give me your blessing.

536
00:54:36,790 --> 00:54:38,290
Take them as a gift.

537
00:54:38,290 --> 00:54:39,510
I can't.

538
00:54:39,510 --> 00:54:41,510
You will get what
you deserve.

539
00:54:42,330 --> 00:54:44,290
If you take less, it's my suffering.

540
00:54:44,290 --> 00:54:46,290
If you take more, it's your suffering.

541
00:54:47,910 --> 00:54:50,460
Don't let either of us suffer.

542
00:54:59,890 --> 00:55:02,650
May Allah give you a nice
working day...

543
00:55:02,930 --> 00:55:04,930
and lot's of halal profit.

544
00:55:05,170 --> 00:55:06,510
Thank you.

545
00:55:09,050 --> 00:55:10,350
Efendi.

546
00:55:20,485 --> 00:55:22,545
Mari! Mari!

547
00:55:24,045 --> 00:55:25,265
Mari, are you alright?

548
00:55:25,265 --> 00:55:26,145
Are you alright?

549
00:55:26,145 --> 00:55:28,145
I'm not!
I'm not!

550
00:55:28,385 --> 00:55:30,245
My stomach...

551
00:55:32,705 --> 00:55:34,025
Here.

552
00:55:37,425 --> 00:55:39,425
You look pale.
Did you catch a cold?

553
00:55:39,505 --> 00:55:41,305
My inside is crushing!

554
00:55:44,965 --> 00:55:46,725
I'm with you.

555
00:55:47,045 --> 00:55:49,085
Turgut, our baby...

556
00:55:49,225 --> 00:55:50,505
Baby is fine.

557
00:55:50,505 --> 00:55:53,075
Speak well.
The baby is good.

558
00:55:56,265 --> 00:55:58,785
Ayşe Hatun's meal...

559
00:56:02,745 --> 00:56:04,085
What?

560
00:56:04,085 --> 00:56:06,085
Mari! Mari!

561
00:56:10,085 --> 00:56:11,445
Mari!

562
00:56:11,445 --> 00:56:13,165
Mari! Turgut Bey!

563
00:56:13,165 --> 00:56:14,345
What's happening here?

564
00:56:14,345 --> 00:56:15,685
Cornelia, I don't know!

565
00:56:15,685 --> 00:56:17,025
I don't know what's wrong.

566
00:56:17,025 --> 00:56:19,025
-Turgut...
-Mari!

567
00:56:19,025 --> 00:56:20,265
Are you alright, my lady?

568
00:56:20,265 --> 00:56:22,265
Turgut, our baby...

569
00:56:23,305 --> 00:56:24,685
It'll be alright.

570
00:56:24,685 --> 00:56:27,225
We'll go to Kumral Abdal.

571
00:56:42,005 --> 00:56:44,045
Doesn't Söğüt have laws?

572
00:56:51,505 --> 00:56:53,045
Why are you intervening?

573
00:56:55,545 --> 00:56:57,365
Who are you? Tell me.

574
00:56:57,905 --> 00:57:00,405
This poor man is İbrahim Fakih.

575
00:57:01,105 --> 00:57:02,865
This is my studend İshak.

576
00:57:05,065 --> 00:57:08,425
It's my duty to correct the
mistakes I witness.

577
00:57:10,905 --> 00:57:14,705
Are you on the wrong side that
you are disturbed?

578
00:57:22,045 --> 00:57:24,545
Do you know who you are
talking to?

579
00:57:26,045 --> 00:57:27,745
You can be a sultan or a bey.

580
00:57:28,525 --> 00:57:30,165
I know what's right and
I speak it.

581
00:57:30,605 --> 00:57:32,225
It doesn't matter.

582
00:57:33,725 --> 00:57:35,925
We need men who speak the truth.

583
00:57:38,245 --> 00:57:40,645
And this poor man is Osman Bey.

584
00:57:42,905 --> 00:57:48,265
Here, this weapon is all I have.

585
00:57:49,905 --> 00:57:51,425
But my weapon...

586
00:57:53,365 --> 00:57:55,505
doesn't let wrongs live
in Söğüt.

587
00:57:57,745 --> 00:57:59,525
Thank you, Osman Bey.

588
00:57:59,625 --> 00:58:00,945
Thank you.

589
00:58:01,225 --> 00:58:02,585
Thank you.

590
00:58:03,825 --> 00:58:05,145
Tell me.

591
00:58:05,405 --> 00:58:07,185
Where are you coming from?

592
00:58:07,185 --> 00:58:08,925
We are coming from Semerkant.

593
00:58:10,645 --> 00:58:13,205
You brought Semerkant's smell to Söğüt.

594
00:58:14,085 --> 00:58:16,125
I'm glad you came, İbrahim Fakih.

595
00:58:16,745 --> 00:58:18,065
Salam Alaikum.

596
00:58:18,065 --> 00:58:19,425
Alaikum Salam.

597
00:58:19,425 --> 00:58:20,945
Welcome, my bey.

598
00:58:20,945 --> 00:58:22,645
Thank you.
Thank you.

599
00:58:22,645 --> 00:58:24,645
We have hot soups.
Come in.

600
00:58:25,045 --> 00:58:26,245
Let's get in.

601
00:58:26,285 --> 00:58:27,345
İbrahim Fakih.

602
00:58:27,345 --> 00:58:28,705
Please.

603
00:58:37,985 --> 00:58:41,745
Less or more, haram is the same, you said.

604
00:58:42,605 --> 00:58:45,125
You saved my shopekeeper
from great pain.

605
00:58:45,425 --> 00:58:47,005
Thank you.

606
00:58:47,845 --> 00:58:52,925
We believe that Allah gives livelihood
to all that is created.

607
00:58:53,245 --> 00:58:56,825
A human's part is searching
for their livelihood in halal ways...

608
00:58:57,125 --> 00:59:00,125
and not follow the devil's path...

609
00:59:00,125 --> 00:59:02,985
and go haram ways to do so.

610
00:59:04,145 --> 00:59:07,025
You spoke greatly.

611
00:59:08,225 --> 00:59:14,425
The devil is the most ancient and cruelest
enemy of the humans.

612
00:59:15,745 --> 00:59:19,965
Muslims should put effort
to not let the devil triumph.

613
00:59:20,605 --> 00:59:22,445
You are right, Osman Bey.

614
00:59:23,385 --> 00:59:27,545
The devil can sway the Muslims.

615
00:59:27,965 --> 00:59:30,045
It can make brothers fight.

616
00:59:32,345 --> 00:59:34,345
It takes such shapes that...

617
00:59:34,565 --> 00:59:36,705
it hides so well that...

618
00:59:37,585 --> 00:59:40,565
it take place between your
eyebrows but...

619
00:59:40,945 --> 00:59:42,985
you still can't see it.

620
00:59:46,505 --> 00:59:49,805
It flows in your veins
like poison...

621
00:59:50,085 --> 00:59:52,005
but you can't know before you bleed.

622
01:00:14,775 --> 01:00:17,835
Help Alps! Help!

623
01:00:18,125 --> 01:00:20,745
Help!

624
01:00:21,285 --> 01:00:26,965
- Help!
- Kumral Abdal, Mother Selcan, help!

625
01:00:28,435 --> 01:00:29,835
Help!

626
01:00:32,525 --> 01:00:34,825
My baby...

627
01:00:36,725 --> 01:00:39,855
I won't leave you or the baby.

628
01:00:40,685 --> 01:00:42,985
Kumral Abdal will heal you.

629
01:00:45,795 --> 01:00:47,095
Mari?

630
01:00:53,045 --> 01:00:54,595
Don't go.

631
01:00:54,865 --> 01:00:56,605
Don't go.

632
01:00:58,595 --> 01:01:00,015
Don't go, darling.

633
01:01:07,105 --> 01:01:08,635
Mari, don't go.

634
01:01:11,135 --> 01:01:12,895
Don't go, darling.

635
01:01:16,605 --> 01:01:18,165
Mari?

636
01:01:29,085 --> 01:01:31,155
- Mari!
- Mari, my girl?

637
01:01:38,205 --> 01:01:39,225
What happened?

638
01:01:48,905 --> 01:01:51,635
Kumral Abdal, tell me something.

639
01:01:53,245 --> 01:01:56,315
Tell me she didn't die,
tell me she's well.

640
01:01:57,165 --> 01:01:58,715
Tell me.

641
01:02:02,785 --> 01:02:05,345
There is nothing we can do, Turgut Bey.

642
01:02:21,825 --> 01:02:23,795
No!

643
01:02:23,795 --> 01:02:25,525
My beautiful!

644
01:02:31,815 --> 01:02:34,195
Wake up my beautiful darling.

645
01:02:34,985 --> 01:02:36,755
Don't go, please!

646
01:02:53,605 --> 01:02:54,905
Please!

647
01:02:58,815 --> 01:03:00,825
I couldn't protect her, mother.

648
01:03:01,935 --> 01:03:04,195
I couldn't protect my hatun and my baby.

649
01:03:05,025 --> 01:03:06,605
What kind of father am I?

650
01:03:07,115 --> 01:03:08,705
What kind of bey am I?

651
01:03:08,705 --> 01:03:11,295
Mother Selcan, I couldn't protect them.

652
01:03:11,475 --> 01:03:13,295
I couldn't protect you.

653
01:03:13,645 --> 01:03:16,165
Don't say that, son. Don't say that.

654
01:03:23,955 --> 01:03:25,795
My beautiful.

655
01:03:28,545 --> 01:03:30,125
I couldn't protect you.

656
01:04:30,285 --> 01:04:31,865
They poisoned her.

657
01:04:35,185 --> 01:04:36,535
They killed her!

658
01:04:36,535 --> 01:04:38,085
They poisoned her!

659
01:04:38,085 --> 01:04:39,625
How could you kill her?

660
01:04:39,625 --> 01:04:41,785
How could you kill her?
How?

661
01:04:41,785 --> 01:04:44,035
You did this!

662
01:04:44,085 --> 01:04:45,665
Cornelia, stop!

663
01:04:45,665 --> 01:04:47,255
What are you saying?

664
01:04:47,275 --> 01:04:49,325
They poisoned her!
They did it!

665
01:04:49,325 --> 01:04:51,125
Why would anyone do that?

666
01:04:51,125 --> 01:04:53,955
They poisoned her! They did!

667
01:04:53,955 --> 01:04:57,005
Know your place, hatun!
What are you saying?

668
01:04:57,655 --> 01:04:59,235
They killed Mari.

669
01:05:27,265 --> 01:05:29,285
You say you come from Semel camp.

670
01:05:30,275 --> 01:05:31,865
Where are you going?

671
01:05:31,915 --> 01:05:34,425
My wish is to go to Contantinniye

672
01:05:34,425 --> 01:05:36,455
We're heading west.

673
01:05:41,255 --> 01:05:43,975
We'd like to establish science in Sogut.

674
01:05:46,685 --> 01:05:48,045
Stay here.

675
01:05:49,355 --> 01:05:51,705
Why would you like me
to stay here, Osman Bey?

676
01:05:58,375 --> 01:06:01,335
There is no establishment of a
government without knowledge.

677
01:06:02,955 --> 01:06:05,515
Of course, we got alfakis and scholars.

678
01:06:05,725 --> 01:06:13,095
But a government that has more
alps than alfakis can never be.

679
01:06:13,955 --> 01:06:15,535
For that reason...

680
01:06:16,835 --> 01:06:18,375
...stay here.

681
01:06:19,645 --> 01:06:22,615
Even if it gets established,
it could not be able to stand.

682
01:06:24,785 --> 01:06:26,545
Science and knowledge.

683
01:06:27,465 --> 01:06:32,265
Without them, the cause of
world conquest is impossible.

684
01:06:33,075 --> 01:06:36,365
When we see the ones that
have the same cause as us...

685
01:06:38,365 --> 01:06:39,965
...we get happy.

686
01:06:43,695 --> 01:06:45,995
May Söğüt be granted with your wisdom.

687
01:06:52,345 --> 01:06:53,695
My Sheikh!

688
01:06:57,635 --> 01:06:59,005
My Sheikh!

689
01:07:02,415 --> 01:07:03,915
Salam aleikum!

690
01:07:04,025 --> 01:07:06,695
Alaikum salam, Osman Bey!

691
01:07:06,695 --> 01:07:13,385
My Sheikh, this is İbrahim Fakih. He came
to Söğüt from Semerkant.

692
01:07:14,195 --> 01:07:15,775
İbrahim Fakih.

693
01:07:17,915 --> 01:07:19,655
İbrahim Fakih.

694
01:07:20,745 --> 01:07:23,435
I don't remember
sending you an invitation.

695
01:07:27,625 --> 01:07:30,355
But welcome anyway.

696
01:07:31,005 --> 01:07:33,595
The light of Oghuz Sheikh Edebalı.

697
01:07:37,225 --> 01:07:39,945
A guest without an invitation is better.

698
01:07:40,195 --> 01:07:43,065
Osman Bey wants me to camp in Söğüt.

699
01:07:44,025 --> 01:07:47,025
Thank Allah for granting
me with meeting you!

700
01:07:47,395 --> 01:07:52,175
I would like to speak to
you longer, İbrahim Fakih.

701
01:07:52,585 --> 01:07:54,675
With pleasure, Sheikh Edebalı.

702
01:07:56,815 --> 01:07:59,115
Akça Dervish made
arrangements in the tavern.

703
01:07:59,545 --> 01:08:01,595
Let's go over there and have a chat.

704
01:08:02,395 --> 01:08:03,775
My Sheikh.

705
01:08:05,975 --> 01:08:07,335
After you.

706
01:08:15,315 --> 01:08:16,845
They poisoned her.

707
01:08:21,925 --> 01:08:26,035
They poisoned my hatun and my baby.

708
01:08:26,345 --> 01:08:28,575
At least, let's get them inside.

709
01:08:29,175 --> 01:08:31,635
We shouldn't keep
them here for all to see.

710
01:08:31,885 --> 01:08:34,925
I promise you, we'll
fınd out who did this.

711
01:08:35,215 --> 01:08:38,285
Come on, let them go. Let them
go so that we can carry them.

712
01:08:38,645 --> 01:08:40,145
Alps!

713
01:08:42,215 --> 01:08:45,215
Let us carry them, come on.

714
01:08:45,625 --> 01:08:47,415
Come on.

715
01:09:35,975 --> 01:09:37,495
Turgut Bey!

716
01:09:38,385 --> 01:09:41,194
Stop!

717
01:09:41,194 --> 01:09:45,734
Don't do it!

718
01:09:46,694 --> 01:09:50,495
Gündüz! Gündüz!

719
01:09:50,765 --> 01:09:53,854
You killed her! You killed Mari!

720
01:09:53,955 --> 01:09:55,805
You killed my baby!

721
01:09:55,805 --> 01:09:59,165
Gündüz, you killed my hatun!

722
01:09:59,475 --> 01:10:03,255
Why Gündüz? Why? Why!?

723
01:10:03,505 --> 01:10:05,585
Why?

724
01:10:05,985 --> 01:10:08,675
What are you saying Turgut?
Why would I do such a thing?

725
01:10:08,885 --> 01:10:11,665
You did it before and did it again!

726
01:10:11,665 --> 01:10:13,835
What do you want from us, Gündüz?

727
01:10:13,835 --> 01:10:15,835
What did you want from me?

728
01:10:24,745 --> 01:10:26,525
See what's going on?

729
01:10:27,225 --> 01:10:29,725
They started falling apart
without us making a move.

730
01:10:34,085 --> 01:10:35,645
I didn't do it.

731
01:10:38,825 --> 01:10:40,195
I didn't do it.

732
01:10:40,595 --> 01:10:42,745
I won't forgive you Gündüz.

733
01:10:45,465 --> 01:10:47,335
Stop Turgut, stop!

734
01:10:47,805 --> 01:10:51,845
How could I stop?
My life is over!

735
01:10:54,955 --> 01:10:58,025
Turgut Bey! Turgut Bey!

736
01:10:59,365 --> 01:11:00,905
Turgut Bey.

737
01:11:03,315 --> 01:11:06,055
The truth will eventually come out.

738
01:11:08,465 --> 01:11:11,335
Don't do anything you may regret later on.

739
01:11:55,295 --> 01:11:56,685
Akça Dervish,...

740
01:11:56,685 --> 01:11:58,590
...praise be! You did a

741
01:11:58,590 --> 01:12:00,495
good job with this place.

742
01:12:02,645 --> 01:12:04,665
You do your job well.

743
01:12:04,945 --> 01:12:06,395
Thank you, Osman Bey!

744
01:12:07,105 --> 01:12:09,485
I try my best.

745
01:12:12,965 --> 01:12:15,285
The food was delicious.

746
01:12:15,285 --> 01:12:16,815
Bless your hands!

747
01:12:17,895 --> 01:12:20,835
I'm happy you enjoyed your meal.

748
01:12:22,085 --> 01:12:27,615
So, you came all the way from Semerkant.

749
01:12:29,265 --> 01:12:32,445
And you are İbrahim Fakih.

750
01:12:34,985 --> 01:12:37,595
What brings you here?

751
01:12:40,885 --> 01:12:45,205
I got many reasons to be
here, Sheikh Edebalı.

752
01:12:45,995 --> 01:12:50,805
I will seek wisdom till the day I die.

753
01:12:52,575 --> 01:12:54,745
Reading is my passion

754
01:12:55,595 --> 01:12:59,025
I read about Ebu Hafs
Necmettin Al Nasafi as well.

755
01:13:05,025 --> 01:13:10,155
Human improves via reading.

756
01:13:11,505 --> 01:13:17,375
You came from Semerkant
and they call you İbrahim Fakih.

757
01:13:19,905 --> 01:13:24,475
It would be better to listen
Alaaddin Semerkandi from you.

758
01:13:38,555 --> 01:13:40,965
I know Alaaddin Semerkandi...

759
01:13:41,345 --> 01:13:44,585
...from my first teacher, my ancestor.

760
01:13:47,765 --> 01:13:52,005
Now, I transfer his information into
my students.

761
01:13:55,085 --> 01:14:00,645
It would be a pleasure for me
to tell you that, Sheikh Edebalı.

762
01:14:07,745 --> 01:14:11,645
If Allah permits, Kayı and Söğüt
will be granted with your wisdom.

763
01:14:17,085 --> 01:14:20,905
"Whoever has knowledge may they share it."

764
01:14:21,385 --> 01:14:23,865
It is a good deed to share
knowledge, Osman Bey.

765
01:14:24,165 --> 01:14:25,705
It would be a pleasure.

766
01:14:28,025 --> 01:14:29,545
- Bey Sungur.
- My bey?

767
01:14:29,725 --> 01:14:31,245
Get the horse ready.

768
01:14:31,285 --> 01:14:32,845
Yes, my bey!

769
01:14:32,905 --> 01:14:36,405
I bid you farewell.

770
01:14:38,465 --> 01:14:39,845
My Sheikh.

771
01:14:53,285 --> 01:14:56,069
İNEGÖL CASTLE

772
01:14:56,585 --> 01:14:58,645
What is going on again, Nikola?

773
01:14:59,245 --> 01:15:01,305
There is a disturbance in your castle.

774
01:15:01,305 --> 01:15:04,625
What do you think
Osman will do now, Koses?

775
01:15:04,625 --> 01:15:07,165
You're the only one
worried about that, it seems.

776
01:15:08,785 --> 01:15:10,305
You tell me.

777
01:15:12,065 --> 01:15:13,645
He entered our castles.

778
01:15:13,765 --> 01:15:16,325
Learned about everything.

779
01:15:17,285 --> 01:15:20,545
Turks take what they explore, Koses.

780
01:15:20,545 --> 01:15:24,245
But you entered all the
way to his tent, Nikola.

781
01:15:24,245 --> 01:15:26,245
I don't want war.

782
01:15:26,285 --> 01:15:28,305
I just want power.

783
01:15:28,305 --> 01:15:29,685
That's it.

784
01:15:29,725 --> 01:15:37,165
But Osman has gotten stronger
by defeating his enemies one by one.

785
01:15:37,265 --> 01:15:38,985
Don't do this Nikola.

786
01:15:39,465 --> 01:15:43,025
Vizier and Geyhatu were
our enemies as well.

787
01:15:43,885 --> 01:15:46,385
Tell me what you really want.

788
01:15:47,445 --> 01:15:48,745
Balance.

789
01:15:50,265 --> 01:15:51,805
I want balance,...

790
01:15:51,805 --> 01:15:53,325
...Koses.

791
01:15:54,085 --> 01:15:55,605
But Osman...

792
01:15:56,305 --> 01:15:59,485
...has upset the balance.

793
01:16:00,985 --> 01:16:04,685
He could attack anytime.

794
01:16:06,425 --> 01:16:07,765
If I remember correctly...

795
01:16:07,865 --> 01:16:12,265
...the same Osman handed me Harmankaya.

796
01:16:13,265 --> 01:16:22,265
The same castle you took from me
by the balance, you set up with Vizier.

797
01:16:22,485 --> 01:16:23,865
That one.

798
01:16:25,185 --> 01:16:30,545
That's why I have no doubt
about who to trust, Nikola.

799
01:16:30,705 --> 01:16:32,045
Don't worry.

800
01:16:32,065 --> 01:16:33,785
You're not aware...

801
01:16:33,965 --> 01:16:35,485
...Koses.

802
01:16:36,625 --> 01:16:43,045
I hope when you do realize,
it won't be too late for you.

803
01:16:44,045 --> 01:16:45,345
Like you said...

804
01:16:45,865 --> 01:16:47,205
...let's stay friends.

805
01:16:47,485 --> 01:16:48,825
For now.

806
01:16:49,805 --> 01:16:53,425
Because the war is at the door.

807
01:17:04,905 --> 01:17:06,905
Would you allow me, mother?

808
01:17:22,045 --> 01:17:24,865
Everything was great with
you, mother of my child.

809
01:17:28,685 --> 01:17:30,425
Everything was great.

810
01:17:57,525 --> 01:18:00,105
Why did our story end
like this, mother Selcan?

811
01:18:00,965 --> 01:18:03,005
What did we do to deserve this?

812
01:18:04,265 --> 01:18:06,045
We'll find out who did this, son.

813
01:18:07,265 --> 01:18:10,345
We'll find who did this, eventually.

814
01:18:23,005 --> 01:18:24,525
She's in your hands.

815
01:18:26,745 --> 01:18:28,745
Look after Mari.

816
01:18:46,205 --> 01:18:47,665
Tell me, Cornelia.

817
01:18:49,385 --> 01:18:51,085
What did Mari eat before she died?

818
01:18:58,805 --> 01:19:00,105
This.

819
01:19:00,445 --> 01:19:01,985
This is it.

820
01:19:03,665 --> 01:19:05,165
She ate this.

821
01:19:06,585 --> 01:19:09,665
Ayşe Hatun gave me this.

822
01:19:24,925 --> 01:19:27,565
Kumral Abdal, Mari ate
that before she died.

823
01:19:29,805 --> 01:19:31,585
Tell us Kumral Abdal...

824
01:19:32,905 --> 01:19:34,445
...tell us something.

825
01:19:34,785 --> 01:19:37,165
Get us out of this dark wellhole

826
01:20:07,425 --> 01:20:08,925
She got poisoned.

827
01:20:14,705 --> 01:20:16,825
It's a very effective poison.

828
01:20:30,825 --> 01:20:33,065
Hide the plate, Kumral Abdal.

829
01:20:33,745 --> 01:20:35,485
Osman Bey would like to see it.

830
01:20:37,025 --> 01:20:39,365
My beautiful Mari.

831
01:20:40,245 --> 01:20:43,065
Was this how you were supposed to die?

832
01:20:45,865 --> 01:20:47,905
Who would kill a pregnant hatun?

833
01:20:48,885 --> 01:20:51,165
Who could be this brutal?

834
01:20:55,665 --> 01:20:58,345
I had nobody besides her.

835
01:21:00,505 --> 01:21:03,505
She was like my sister.

836
01:21:15,025 --> 01:21:16,765
Ayşe Hatun.

837
01:21:18,985 --> 01:21:22,545
Is this the plate you gave?

838
01:21:28,825 --> 01:21:30,205
Ayşe?

839
01:21:30,425 --> 01:21:32,285
I didn't do it, mother.

840
01:21:38,305 --> 01:21:39,885
I didn't do it.

841
01:21:41,345 --> 01:21:42,885
You say Mari.

842
01:21:42,985 --> 01:21:44,485
Mari.

843
01:21:45,245 --> 01:21:46,645
Pregnant Mari.

844
01:21:47,745 --> 01:21:50,265
How could I kill Mari?

845
01:21:51,625 --> 01:21:54,445
How could I kill an unborn baby?

846
01:21:57,545 --> 01:21:59,565
I swear, I didn't do it.

847
01:22:00,565 --> 01:22:02,125
If Allah permits.

848
01:22:04,345 --> 01:22:05,925
If Allah permits.

849
01:22:18,745 --> 01:22:20,805
The messenger on the road...

850
01:22:21,505 --> 01:22:23,325
...why is it, Nikola?

851
01:22:23,465 --> 01:22:25,825
To let the emperor know of my opinions.

852
01:22:25,865 --> 01:22:27,425
Also,...

853
01:22:27,425 --> 01:22:28,985
...Geyhatu is gone.

854
01:22:29,285 --> 01:22:33,145
The deal is over.

855
01:22:33,545 --> 01:22:34,845
That's true.

856
01:22:35,505 --> 01:22:38,225
Instead of making a new deal...

857
01:22:38,745 --> 01:22:40,345
...you want war.

858
01:22:42,145 --> 01:22:43,705
It's not me who wants war.

859
01:22:44,285 --> 01:22:46,425
Osman. Osman himself.

860
01:22:46,425 --> 01:22:47,925
Osman.

861
01:22:51,540 --> 01:22:53,100
Soldier.

862
01:22:53,380 --> 01:22:54,940
Kayı Bey Osman Bey is coming.

863
01:22:54,940 --> 01:22:56,940
Quickly, soldier! Quickly!

864
01:23:17,440 --> 01:23:19,000
Osman Bey!

865
01:23:19,360 --> 01:23:20,920
Welcome!

866
01:23:23,520 --> 01:23:25,540
Happy to be here, Nikola!

867
01:23:26,600 --> 01:23:28,180
Happy to be here!

868
01:23:29,885 --> 01:23:32,045
What is the state of these roads, Nikola?

869
01:23:33,525 --> 01:23:35,605
There are soldiers everywhere.

870
01:23:36,925 --> 01:23:38,285
Caution.

871
01:23:38,625 --> 01:23:40,425
I like caution.

872
01:23:41,225 --> 01:23:43,505
Is it because of us?

873
01:23:45,685 --> 01:23:47,625
If so, let us know.

874
01:23:48,445 --> 01:23:50,745
We'll act accordingly.

875
01:23:50,745 --> 01:23:52,745
Of course not, Osman Bey.

876
01:23:53,845 --> 01:23:56,185
We're friends now.

877
01:23:56,785 --> 01:23:58,105
If that was the case...

878
01:23:58,625 --> 01:24:02,905
...could you get into
this castle like this?

879
01:24:04,145 --> 01:24:05,765
Let's say you did.

880
01:24:06,045 --> 01:24:11,485
Could you leave with no harm?

881
01:24:12,925 --> 01:24:14,345
I could.

882
01:24:18,045 --> 01:24:20,985
I did it before.

883
01:24:23,325 --> 01:24:25,205
If I were to take it...

884
01:24:27,605 --> 01:24:29,385
...you would hear the rumble.

885
01:24:40,045 --> 01:24:41,785
How could Turgut Bey do that?

886
01:24:42,925 --> 01:24:45,945
Why would Gündüz Bey
want to hurt Mari Hatun?

887
01:24:46,265 --> 01:24:48,765
He doesn't know what he's doing, Cerkutay.

888
01:24:52,945 --> 01:24:55,305
This is the hardest test one can have.

889
01:24:56,345 --> 01:24:58,485
He suffers real bad.

890
01:25:00,045 --> 01:25:02,765
May Allah never grant that
type of suffering on anybody.

891
01:25:02,825 --> 01:25:05,525
Nobody can bear that type of suffering.

892
01:25:08,985 --> 01:25:10,365
You're right.

893
01:25:10,905 --> 01:25:12,625
He's really hurt.

894
01:25:15,845 --> 01:25:17,225
But...

895
01:25:17,705 --> 01:25:19,285
...Gündüz Bey,...

896
01:25:20,985 --> 01:25:22,545
...Ayşe Hatun,...

897
01:25:25,485 --> 01:25:26,845
...I don't know.

898
01:25:27,365 --> 01:25:29,125
Would they ever do such a thing?

899
01:25:34,865 --> 01:25:36,905
One side of me says no...

900
01:25:37,365 --> 01:25:42,065
...but wasn't it a short time ago
when they handed Mari to Vizier?

901
01:25:46,385 --> 01:25:48,765
I hope that's not the case.

902
01:26:06,525 --> 01:26:08,105
Sister!

903
01:26:09,365 --> 01:26:10,745
Stop!

904
01:26:23,985 --> 01:26:28,665
I don't think we need war or rumble.

905
01:26:29,745 --> 01:26:33,245
We're the men that
destroyed Vizier and Geyhatu.

906
01:26:34,085 --> 01:26:36,085
Peace be with us.

907
01:26:36,525 --> 01:26:38,025
Exactly!

908
01:26:38,565 --> 01:26:41,105
As Koses says, Osman Bey...

909
01:26:41,105 --> 01:26:43,745
...war shouldn't even be the discussion.

910
01:26:44,485 --> 01:26:45,565
Right?

911
01:26:47,485 --> 01:26:49,365
Argus, quickly!

912
01:26:49,365 --> 01:26:50,765
Tell our cooks...

913
01:26:50,765 --> 01:26:54,945
...to arrange a table for Koses
and Osman Bey, quickly!

914
01:26:55,705 --> 01:26:57,765
No.

915
01:26:59,225 --> 01:27:00,745
I won't stay to eat.

916
01:27:03,665 --> 01:27:05,045
I'm heading to the tent.

917
01:27:05,765 --> 01:27:07,805
I'm coming with you, Osman Bey.

918
01:27:22,155 --> 01:27:24,485
He still looks me in the eye.

919
01:27:25,595 --> 01:27:26,925
Has no shame.

920
01:27:29,195 --> 01:27:30,525
Still.

921
01:27:34,125 --> 01:27:36,005
We'll find it out.

922
01:27:36,935 --> 01:27:40,295
But, I told you, Turgut Bey.

923
01:27:42,165 --> 01:27:43,945
I'll tell you again.

924
01:27:44,225 --> 01:27:45,935
You're full of rage.

925
01:27:47,375 --> 01:27:50,005
If it's you Gündüz...

926
01:27:55,225 --> 01:27:57,015
...if it's you...

927
01:27:59,315 --> 01:28:02,405
...I will end you with Mari's dagger.

928
01:28:04,455 --> 01:28:06,355
If it's you.

929
01:28:09,085 --> 01:28:12,165
What kind of poison is that, Gündüz Bey?

930
01:28:12,325 --> 01:28:14,085
I didn't do it, Bala Hatun.

931
01:28:14,245 --> 01:28:15,595
I didn't do it!

932
01:28:15,985 --> 01:28:18,595
Don't you see what kind
of slander I fall victim to?

933
01:28:20,355 --> 01:28:21,625
I didn't do it.

934
01:28:42,775 --> 01:28:45,115
Tell me Kumral Abdal.

935
01:28:46,645 --> 01:28:48,985
Look into my eyes and tell me.

936
01:28:52,145 --> 01:28:53,685
What happened to my Mari?

937
01:28:54,115 --> 01:28:56,225
What happened to my baby?

938
01:28:57,665 --> 01:28:59,665
Tell me, Kumral Abdal.

939
01:29:04,915 --> 01:29:07,205
The food was poisonous.

940
01:29:14,295 --> 01:29:15,965
The baby died first...

941
01:29:19,235 --> 01:29:21,505
...then, Mari Hatun.

942
01:29:36,025 --> 01:29:39,305
The poison that came out of the food...

943
01:29:42,065 --> 01:29:44,835
...was found in Gündüz Bey's tent.

944
01:29:59,225 --> 01:30:00,525
Stop!

945
01:30:00,525 --> 01:30:01,895
Turgut Bey!

946
01:30:01,895 --> 01:30:04,405
Turgut Bey! Turgut Bey don't!

947
01:30:06,665 --> 01:30:09,755
Turgut Bey! Turgut Bey!
Stop!

948
01:30:10,125 --> 01:30:12,825
Turgut Bey! Don't! Please!

949
01:30:14,865 --> 01:30:16,385
Turgut Bey!

950
01:30:19,255 --> 01:30:21,045
What is happening here?

951
01:30:23,085 --> 01:30:24,605
Turgut Bey!

952
01:30:24,665 --> 01:30:26,255
Turgut Bey!

953
01:30:26,505 --> 01:30:28,765
What is happening here?
Stop!

954
01:30:29,005 --> 01:30:30,525
Turgut Bey!

955
01:30:30,545 --> 01:30:32,055
What is this?

956
01:30:32,125 --> 01:30:33,715
What is happening here?

957
01:30:33,785 --> 01:30:35,145
Tell me!

958
01:30:35,585 --> 01:30:37,125
Turgut!

959
01:30:37,265 --> 01:30:38,805
Turgut!

960
01:30:39,685 --> 01:30:42,225
This man you call brother...

961
01:30:42,265 --> 01:30:44,145
...took my wife!

962
01:30:44,145 --> 01:30:46,215
He took my life!

963
01:30:46,245 --> 01:30:47,565
What are you saying?

964
01:30:47,565 --> 01:30:49,865
He cut my breath!

965
01:30:52,165 --> 01:30:54,665
I will cut your breath too, Gündüz Bey!

966
01:30:54,875 --> 01:30:57,075
I will end you, Gündüz Bey!

967
01:30:57,075 --> 01:31:00,085
You are done!

968
01:31:00,085 --> 01:31:02,165
You are making no sense right now.

969
01:31:08,675 --> 01:31:10,955
Turgut! Turgut!

970
01:31:11,735 --> 01:31:12,945
Mari!

971
01:31:14,455 --> 01:31:15,805
Mari!

972
01:31:18,145 --> 01:31:19,665
Mari!

973
01:31:23,205 --> 01:31:25,245
Is this true, brother?

974
01:31:26,705 --> 01:31:28,225
Brother!

975
01:31:32,585 --> 01:31:34,285
I didn't. I didn't

976
01:31:34,285 --> 01:31:36,825
You are lying!

977
01:31:36,825 --> 01:31:39,285
You are lying, Gündüz!

978
01:31:39,285 --> 01:31:41,265
You are lying to me!

979
01:31:41,265 --> 01:31:43,625
You took my Mari away from me!

980
01:31:50,645 --> 01:31:51,665
Turgut!

981
01:31:52,605 --> 01:31:53,725
Turgut!

982
01:31:55,425 --> 01:31:56,695
Stop for a moment!

983
01:32:00,845 --> 01:32:06,015
Take my brother to the prisoner tent
for now!

984
01:32:07,245 --> 01:32:08,625
Come on!

985
01:32:08,625 --> 01:32:10,195
No, Osman Bey!

986
01:32:10,195 --> 01:32:13,225
Let me, let me go!

987
01:32:13,425 --> 01:32:19,005
-My Mari! My Mari!
-Calm down! Calm down!

988
01:32:19,005 --> 01:32:21,685
Turgut! Stop!

989
01:32:22,425 --> 01:32:23,865
Brother...

990
01:32:24,065 --> 01:32:25,635
...stop for a second!

991
01:32:28,385 --> 01:32:30,445
Stop for a second!

992
01:32:30,665 --> 01:32:32,005
Stop for a second.

993
01:32:32,255 --> 01:32:33,625
Stop for a second.

994
01:32:53,255 --> 01:32:54,805
Brother!

995
01:33:13,125 --> 01:33:14,645
I am so sorry.

996
01:33:18,085 --> 01:33:19,395
But...

997
01:33:20,725 --> 01:33:23,745
...you died for a very important cause.

998
01:33:31,205 --> 01:33:36,185
I will pray for you until my last breath.

999
01:33:45,050 --> 01:33:46,440
Mari!

1000
01:33:53,685 --> 01:33:55,035
Get out.

1001
01:34:43,415 --> 01:34:44,715
I am sorry!

1002
01:35:10,115 --> 01:35:11,685
Forgive me!

1003
01:35:17,555 --> 01:35:19,775
I left you alone!

1004
01:35:24,325 --> 01:35:26,135
But look, I am here now!

1005
01:35:26,825 --> 01:35:28,925
Your brother is here.

1006
01:35:29,265 --> 01:35:31,465
Let's go home.

1007
01:35:36,095 --> 01:35:39,975
I promise you I will never let anyone
hurt you again!

1008
01:35:45,435 --> 01:35:47,335
Please, Mari!

1009
01:35:49,295 --> 01:35:51,515
Please don't leave me.

1010
01:35:55,385 --> 01:35:57,815
You are my only family!

1011
01:36:01,775 --> 01:36:03,775
Come on, we are going home.

1012
01:36:05,235 --> 01:36:06,495
Wake up.

1013
01:36:07,725 --> 01:36:09,275
Please!

1014
01:36:43,995 --> 01:36:46,005
I won't give you my sister.

1015
01:37:10,665 --> 01:37:11,985
I won't!

1016
01:37:18,995 --> 01:37:22,225
Hatuns, try to remember.

1017
01:37:22,635 --> 01:37:27,485
Didn't you see anyone strange in the tribe
or near Gündüz Bey's tent?

1018
01:37:27,555 --> 01:37:28,915
No.

1019
01:37:29,905 --> 01:37:31,275
No.

1020
01:37:32,215 --> 01:37:34,525
Didn't you suspect anyone?

1021
01:37:35,135 --> 01:37:36,645
None?

1022
01:37:36,735 --> 01:37:38,595
We didn't see anyone, Bala Hatun.

1023
01:37:41,575 --> 01:37:43,135
Now leave.

1024
01:37:43,335 --> 01:37:44,995
Try hard to remember.

1025
01:37:45,295 --> 01:37:47,605
Come to me at once if you remember
anything.

1026
01:37:47,655 --> 01:37:48,815
Come on.

1027
01:37:48,815 --> 01:37:50,605
All right, Bala Hatun.

1028
01:37:55,485 --> 01:37:57,555
All the evidence lead to them.

1029
01:37:58,715 --> 01:38:00,275
What if they did it?

1030
01:38:01,715 --> 01:38:03,735
We couldn't protect her.

1031
01:38:03,735 --> 01:38:06,735
Aygül, stop saying that!

1032
01:38:07,355 --> 01:38:11,175
Neither Gündüz nor Ayşe would do such
evil, I know it!

1033
01:38:12,685 --> 01:38:14,195
I hope so.

1034
01:38:18,585 --> 01:38:20,635
What is this, mother?

1035
01:38:26,285 --> 01:38:27,625
Son...

1036
01:38:28,155 --> 01:38:30,365
...I will go talk to him again, all right?

1037
01:38:43,840 --> 01:38:45,940
Poison was on the plate...

1038
01:38:47,070 --> 01:38:49,420
...the bottle was in their tent.

1039
01:38:52,890 --> 01:38:55,280
Everything leads to my brother.

1040
01:38:59,560 --> 01:39:00,750
But...

1041
01:39:03,360 --> 01:39:05,560
...my brother...

1042
01:39:06,450 --> 01:39:10,560
...would never do such a thing to a
pregnant woman!

1043
01:39:10,770 --> 01:39:11,950
No way!

1044
01:39:13,310 --> 01:39:15,240
No way he would do it!

1045
01:39:23,720 --> 01:39:25,250
You are right, my Bey.

1046
01:39:26,980 --> 01:39:29,450
But don't forget his latest actions.

1047
01:39:30,770 --> 01:39:32,880
He separated Malhun from her baby.

1048
01:39:33,520 --> 01:39:35,460
He exiled us from the tribe.

1049
01:39:36,770 --> 01:39:40,140
He delivered Mari to the Vizier.

1050
01:39:43,720 --> 01:39:47,310
My father turned out to be a traitor.

1051
01:39:47,770 --> 01:39:49,620
No one surprises me anymore.

1052
01:39:54,360 --> 01:39:56,170
What do the hatuns say?

1053
01:39:56,550 --> 01:39:58,060
Did they see anything?

1054
01:39:58,060 --> 01:39:59,260
No, my Bey.

1055
01:39:59,260 --> 01:40:01,260
No one saw anything.

1056
01:40:14,840 --> 01:40:16,340
I am fine, Ayşe.

1057
01:40:16,340 --> 01:40:17,660
I am fine.

1058
01:40:26,410 --> 01:40:29,480
How could this happen to us, Gündüz?

1059
01:40:31,200 --> 01:40:33,260
We didn't hurt anyone.

1060
01:40:34,950 --> 01:40:37,020
Who did this to us?

1061
01:40:38,210 --> 01:40:41,050
Whoever benefits from killing Mari...

1062
01:40:41,350 --> 01:40:43,900
...and blaming us did it.

1063
01:40:48,400 --> 01:40:50,780
May my Allah save us from this slander,
my Ayşe.

1064
01:40:52,650 --> 01:40:54,210
Amen.

1065
01:41:18,070 --> 01:41:19,430
She is gone.

1066
01:41:21,210 --> 01:41:26,330
Mari is gone, with an innocent baby.

1067
01:41:32,470 --> 01:41:33,850
Tell me, Gündüz.

1068
01:41:35,720 --> 01:41:37,810
Can you be this evil?

1069
01:41:40,410 --> 01:41:42,180
I didn't do it, mother.

1070
01:41:43,960 --> 01:41:45,980
Would I ever hurt a pregnant woman?

1071
01:41:47,860 --> 01:41:49,640
You did before.

1072
01:41:51,770 --> 01:41:54,340
Didn't you send Mari yourself?

1073
01:41:57,910 --> 01:41:59,470
What should I do?

1074
01:41:59,930 --> 01:42:02,440
What should I do, what should I say now?

1075
01:42:08,690 --> 01:42:15,340
What kind of evil is killing an innocent
woman who carries a baby?

1076
01:42:15,340 --> 01:42:18,390
How can you think I would do such an evil,
mother?

1077
01:42:19,640 --> 01:42:20,760
Especially Ayşe.

1078
01:42:26,790 --> 01:42:28,320
I am so sorry about Marİ.

1079
01:42:29,490 --> 01:42:31,070
My heart is burning for her.

1080
01:42:31,770 --> 01:42:34,830
But Allah is my witness I am not involved
in this.

1081
01:42:36,400 --> 01:42:37,970
Know that if I find who did it...

1082
01:42:38,610 --> 01:42:40,710
...I will kill them myself.

1083
01:42:42,100 --> 01:42:45,120
We had just knitted booties for her baby.

1084
01:42:46,940 --> 01:42:48,970
She was so happy, mother.

1085
01:42:51,330 --> 01:42:53,390
Pregnancy looked beautiful on her.

1086
01:42:54,260 --> 01:42:56,420
What kind of an evil is this, mother?

1087
01:42:59,600 --> 01:43:01,950
Don't, my Ayşe.

1088
01:43:06,350 --> 01:43:07,700
Don't.

1089
01:43:21,680 --> 01:43:23,990
What do we do now?

1090
01:43:30,210 --> 01:43:32,310
This doesn't make sense, my Bey.

1091
01:43:32,310 --> 01:43:36,400
Would Gündüz Bey do this in the open if he
wanted to kill Mari?

1092
01:43:37,250 --> 01:43:40,270
He wouldn't. He wouldn't, Bala!

1093
01:43:42,580 --> 01:43:44,610
I agree with you.

1094
01:43:45,650 --> 01:43:48,700
Something doesn't sit right with me.

1095
01:43:51,960 --> 01:43:53,510
My only wish is that...

1096
01:43:55,370 --> 01:43:57,390
...you find them.

1097
01:43:59,810 --> 01:44:04,380
I won't let this incident stop
the conquest.

1098
01:44:05,680 --> 01:44:07,400
The preparations will continue.

1099
01:44:07,770 --> 01:44:09,520
While there is a traitor among us?

1100
01:44:10,320 --> 01:44:12,580
If it is Gündüz, he must have leaked
everything.

1101
01:44:13,650 --> 01:44:15,920
If it is someone else, they are already
outside.

1102
01:44:24,700 --> 01:44:26,850
This is what the enemy wants.

1103
01:44:31,540 --> 01:44:35,540
Maybe this is what it is all about.

1104
01:44:39,700 --> 01:44:42,090
I won't make them happy.

1105
01:44:46,790 --> 01:44:49,410
The conquest will continue no matter
what.

1106
01:44:53,060 --> 01:44:55,570
You will find those traitors.

1107
01:44:58,300 --> 01:45:01,870
My Süleyman Şah's trust is in worthy
hands.

1108
01:45:03,510 --> 01:45:05,680
Everyone can walk on a straight road, son.

1109
01:45:07,000 --> 01:45:09,480
But only those who are brave like
Osman Bey...

1110
01:45:09,580 --> 01:45:12,610
...can walk these bumpy roads.

1111
01:45:16,010 --> 01:45:18,940
Your word is an order for us, my Bey.

1112
01:45:18,940 --> 01:45:21,250
We will certainly find the traitor.

1113
01:45:24,240 --> 01:45:25,610
We will.

1114
01:45:27,310 --> 01:45:28,810
We will, mother.

1115
01:45:40,185 --> 01:45:43,505
Apple, red apple.

1116
01:45:45,465 --> 01:45:50,355
You are a Turk. This is more than an apple
for Turks.

1117
01:45:54,135 --> 01:45:56,455
The red apple symbolizes a dream.

1118
01:45:59,535 --> 01:46:01,035
A far-away dream.

1119
01:46:02,615 --> 01:46:04,725
A dream impossible to reach.

1120
01:46:05,715 --> 01:46:07,025
Good.

1121
01:46:07,855 --> 01:46:10,885
You are with me because your mind works
different from them.

1122
01:46:11,045 --> 01:46:13,955
You are after the reality, not the dream.

1123
01:46:14,265 --> 01:46:19,685
I want a state ruled by fear,
growing as its people fear it.

1124
01:46:20,415 --> 01:46:23,745
So, my way is your way.

1125
01:46:24,575 --> 01:46:26,115
A dark way.

1126
01:46:28,435 --> 01:46:30,765
And we are moving forward.

1127
01:46:31,445 --> 01:46:35,365
Mari is dead, Gündüz is imprisoned.

1128
01:46:36,025 --> 01:46:40,355
Kosses, Turgut... All of them are about to
turn against Osman.

1129
01:46:41,225 --> 01:46:42,815
Everything goes as we wish.

1130
01:46:42,815 --> 01:46:44,255
Not enough!

1131
01:46:46,995 --> 01:46:49,905
What keeps them together is a dream.

1132
01:46:51,235 --> 01:46:54,155
And we will crash that dream.

1133
01:47:02,795 --> 01:47:06,135
A Şed Ceremony will be held in the tavern.

1134
01:47:07,305 --> 01:47:09,455
We will destroy that place.

1135
01:47:11,575 --> 01:47:14,385
We will not only kill them but also...

1136
01:47:14,785 --> 01:47:16,125
...we'll be there...

1137
01:47:16,125 --> 01:47:22,025
...cry for them and eat their halvah.

1138
01:47:32,995 --> 01:47:37,165
Keeping us here and Gündüz there won't
work out, Osman Bey!

1139
01:47:37,515 --> 01:47:40,545
I will bury my sister with her baby
in her womb!

1140
01:47:40,925 --> 01:47:44,395
Just say whatever you will and do whatever
you will do!

1141
01:48:07,585 --> 01:48:10,155
I don't believe my brother did
such a thing.

1142
01:48:13,725 --> 01:48:15,505
What are you saying, Osman Bey?

1143
01:48:17,405 --> 01:48:21,915
Did you forget what he had done when you
entrusted him your tribe?

1144
01:48:24,545 --> 01:48:26,885
And then what he had done to my Mari.

1145
01:48:31,595 --> 01:48:34,985
It's all out there! How can you not think?

1146
01:48:35,705 --> 01:48:37,205
I say I don't think so.

1147
01:48:39,205 --> 01:48:40,685
I am not saying I am sure.

1148
01:48:47,105 --> 01:48:48,975
The justice will be given!

1149
01:48:49,475 --> 01:48:50,895
What is justice?

1150
01:48:55,915 --> 01:48:59,905
Tell me, Osman Bey, what is justice?

1151
01:49:01,285 --> 01:49:03,885
Didn't the poison come out of Gündüz's
tent?

1152
01:49:04,885 --> 01:49:06,855
What proof are we looking for?

1153
01:49:09,365 --> 01:49:12,655
When it comes to your brother,
the scales of your justice...

1154
01:49:13,635 --> 01:49:20,045
...which you do not stop speaking of,
do not be disturbed!

1155
01:49:24,925 --> 01:49:30,720
I am the nation of the prophet who
said that...

1156
01:49:30,720 --> 01:49:36,160
...he will not even favor his children
so that the right will be found.

1157
01:49:42,525 --> 01:49:49,195
Even if it is my brother ow my own
child...

1158
01:49:50,595 --> 01:49:52,955
...I show no mercy.

1159
01:49:57,655 --> 01:50:02,195
I do what is right.

1160
01:50:04,625 --> 01:50:06,115
Then do!

1161
01:50:07,515 --> 01:50:09,685
Speak frankly, Osman Bey.

1162
01:50:11,775 --> 01:50:15,845
Why do you think that Gündüz didn't do it?

1163
01:50:16,515 --> 01:50:18,555
Tell us if you know anything.

1164
01:50:24,435 --> 01:50:27,245
You all know about the problems between
me and my brother.

1165
01:50:28,155 --> 01:50:29,785
Everyone does.

1166
01:50:31,645 --> 01:50:34,025
All this time you've been holding back
your anger.

1167
01:50:35,175 --> 01:50:36,415
I know that too.

1168
01:50:36,995 --> 01:50:50,505
But those who want to hurt Kayı will try
to use the beys first.

1169
01:50:52,425 --> 01:50:53,815
How?

1170
01:50:59,375 --> 01:51:05,535
They killed my Mari to harm your tribe.

1171
01:51:09,655 --> 01:51:11,235
Are you telling me this?

1172
01:51:19,375 --> 01:51:24,925
I can't judge this issue.

1173
01:51:33,095 --> 01:51:34,445
Be patient.

1174
01:51:38,105 --> 01:51:39,645
Kosses...

1175
01:51:41,365 --> 01:51:42,955
...be patient.

1176
01:52:03,510 --> 01:52:06,079
Söğüt

1177
01:52:11,585 --> 01:52:12,955
Enjoy.

1178
01:52:19,685 --> 01:52:23,287
You've been hiding in Söğüt for years and
they never suspected any of you.

1179
01:52:23,755 --> 01:52:26,555
Because you are the children of darkness.

1180
01:52:28,835 --> 01:52:31,375
You made them believe in your loyalty.

1181
01:52:31,975 --> 01:52:34,875
It is time. Söğüt will burn.

1182
01:52:36,715 --> 01:52:39,435
Gunpowder is in apple sacks.

1183
01:52:40,835 --> 01:52:43,215
You will carry sacks of apples here.

1184
01:52:45,415 --> 01:52:48,635
As they think they are meeting
the Şed Ceremony...

1185
01:52:49,755 --> 01:52:51,815
...they will be torn into pieces.

1186
01:52:53,515 --> 01:52:55,075
Quick!

1187
01:52:56,855 --> 01:52:58,435
Hurry up!

1188
01:53:00,435 --> 01:53:01,735
Give it to me.

1189
01:53:04,115 --> 01:53:05,695
All right, go.

1190
01:53:20,285 --> 01:53:23,405
Nothing will stop the conquest.

1191
01:53:26,845 --> 01:53:30,665
You will deploy the archers
on the mountain.

1192
01:53:30,665 --> 01:53:32,185
Sure, my Bey.

1193
01:53:33,185 --> 01:53:34,905
If help comes and...

1194
01:53:35,365 --> 01:53:37,885
...we seem to be taking over
İnhisar...

1195
01:53:38,865 --> 01:53:41,385
...we will get around it first.

1196
01:53:41,505 --> 01:53:43,045
As you order, my Bey.

1197
01:53:43,045 --> 01:53:45,885
Horsemen are ready to strike
the incoming caravans.

1198
01:53:47,085 --> 01:53:48,245
My Bey...

1199
01:53:50,105 --> 01:53:51,385
...İnhisar is asleep.

1200
01:53:51,585 --> 01:53:54,125
There is no one but a few patrols on
the roads.

1201
01:53:54,625 --> 01:53:55,945
As you wished so.

1202
01:53:56,225 --> 01:53:59,805
Two alps are waiting in İnhisar according
to your order.

1203
01:54:01,625 --> 01:54:04,125
Then we will go to İnhisar immediately.

1204
01:54:04,385 --> 01:54:08,165
If you come across something that you can
solve by talking...

1205
01:54:08,765 --> 01:54:10,985
...don't ever touch your swords.

1206
01:54:11,845 --> 01:54:15,525
We will go as shadow and...

1207
01:54:16,465 --> 01:54:18,705
...destroy like a hurricane.

1208
01:54:19,825 --> 01:54:21,185
But...

1209
01:54:21,885 --> 01:54:23,965
...to build a home.

1210
01:54:24,705 --> 01:54:26,465
Right, Akça?

1211
01:54:27,485 --> 01:54:29,185
This is a conquest, my Bey.

1212
01:54:30,385 --> 01:54:32,905
We restore the place we conquer.

1213
01:54:32,925 --> 01:54:34,805
We do!

1214
01:54:37,665 --> 01:54:40,205
You will come with me, Akça.

1215
01:54:40,205 --> 01:54:42,205
We will go after them.

1216
01:54:42,845 --> 01:54:44,425
We will have your Şed Ceremony...

1217
01:54:45,645 --> 01:54:48,205
...before the conquest.

1218
01:54:50,745 --> 01:54:53,885
It suits such a virtuous master!

1219
01:54:55,485 --> 01:54:56,805
Come on.

1220
01:54:58,625 --> 01:55:02,025
You will leave some of the alps here for
guarding.

1221
01:55:03,745 --> 01:55:05,945
We will go to Mari's funeral first.

1222
01:55:07,385 --> 01:55:08,965
After there...

1223
01:55:10,005 --> 01:55:12,525
...we will go to the Şed Ceremony.

1224
01:55:13,505 --> 01:55:15,245
As you order, my Bey.

1225
01:55:17,850 --> 01:55:20,569
Harmankaya Castle

1226
01:55:24,785 --> 01:55:27,365
I swear to my Allah that...

1227
01:55:28,685 --> 01:55:30,945
...I will inflict the worst pain in the
world...

1228
01:55:32,325 --> 01:55:34,525
...on the traitors who took you
away from me...

1229
01:55:34,605 --> 01:55:38,145
...killed our unborn child,
and made you suffer...

1230
01:55:38,805 --> 01:55:41,365
...in front of my eyes.

1231
01:55:51,345 --> 01:55:53,345
But my pain stays.

1232
01:55:55,585 --> 01:55:56,925
It always will.

1233
01:56:35,575 --> 01:56:38,195
I trusted you with my sister.

1234
01:56:38,895 --> 01:56:41,935
You told me not to worry.

1235
01:56:50,485 --> 01:56:54,045
Is this your loyalty?
Is this your love?

1236
01:56:56,225 --> 01:56:58,285
You couldn't protect her!

1237
01:57:00,445 --> 01:57:02,285
You couldn't protect her!

1238
01:57:10,385 --> 01:57:15,485
They killed my sister and my nephew!

1239
01:57:16,325 --> 01:57:18,665
I won't let them get away with this!

1240
01:57:19,745 --> 01:57:21,645
We won't, Kosses.

1241
01:57:24,945 --> 01:57:26,665
We won't.

1242
01:57:30,105 --> 01:57:36,885
I will kill everyone who took her from me
with my own hands!

1243
01:57:37,805 --> 01:57:40,125
You won't do it alone.

1244
01:57:43,905 --> 01:57:45,625
Together.

1245
01:57:47,665 --> 01:57:48,965
Together.

1246
01:57:55,545 --> 01:57:57,725
I don't understand at all.

1247
01:57:58,005 --> 01:58:02,085
How can a man like Gündüz Bey kill
a woman?

1248
01:58:04,565 --> 01:58:07,985
I know the limits of Gündüz's anger well.

1249
01:58:09,865 --> 01:58:12,425
Does he do evil?
He does.

1250
01:58:12,885 --> 01:58:15,405
People...

1251
01:58:16,545 --> 01:58:20,625
But I also know that Gündüz wouldn't be
able to look me in the eyes like that...

1252
01:58:20,905 --> 01:58:23,645
...if he had hurt Mari.

1253
01:58:24,085 --> 01:58:25,885
I don't know them as much as you do.

1254
01:58:27,605 --> 01:58:29,525
But I've heard what he had done.

1255
01:58:31,705 --> 01:58:33,745
Besides, all the evidence lead to them.

1256
01:58:35,265 --> 01:58:37,325
Let's say they did it.

1257
01:58:39,945 --> 01:58:42,845
Why would they leave the bottle in
the tent?

1258
01:58:44,245 --> 01:58:46,205
A smart person wouldn't.

1259
01:58:46,445 --> 01:58:48,505
You are also right, Bala Hatun.

1260
01:58:49,005 --> 01:58:50,165
But...

1261
01:58:50,425 --> 01:58:52,385
...Gündüz Bey may have considered this.

1262
01:58:55,505 --> 01:58:59,065
We will solve this in a short time.

1263
01:58:59,505 --> 01:59:01,365
But we are late for the Şed Ceremony.

1264
01:59:01,365 --> 01:59:02,705
Come on, hatuns.

1265
01:59:02,705 --> 01:59:04,285
Wait, girl.

1266
01:59:04,585 --> 01:59:07,665
Don't you hear me? I am telling you I am
waiting for someone.

1267
01:59:08,885 --> 01:59:10,725
Who is this important person?

1268
01:59:10,745 --> 01:59:12,505
What are you hiding from me?

1269
01:59:12,525 --> 01:59:14,305
Can I come in?

1270
01:59:14,565 --> 01:59:16,065
Come in, girl!

1271
01:59:21,325 --> 01:59:23,885
They are here, Selcen Mother.

1272
01:59:25,505 --> 01:59:27,245
Who is it?

1273
01:59:28,325 --> 01:59:31,125
You are too curious, Aygül.

1274
01:59:31,125 --> 01:59:33,125
You will see when they come.

1275
01:59:33,785 --> 01:59:35,845
Stop bothering me.

1276
01:59:39,085 --> 01:59:41,665
Something is up with you since
the morning.

1277
01:59:43,245 --> 01:59:45,825
Do you know who it is?

1278
02:00:11,365 --> 02:00:12,865
Kayı.

1279
02:00:18,245 --> 02:00:19,945
Run to your mother.

1280
02:00:20,645 --> 02:00:22,005
Son!

1281
02:00:28,425 --> 02:00:29,725
My son!

1282
02:00:31,225 --> 02:00:32,585
Mother!

1283
02:00:39,005 --> 02:00:40,365
Oh, my son!

1284
02:00:48,925 --> 02:00:50,225
My dear!

1285
02:00:50,325 --> 02:00:52,325
My dear son!

1286
02:00:52,805 --> 02:00:54,885
I missed you so much, baby.

1287
02:01:35,485 --> 02:01:37,225
Where's apple are these?

1288
02:01:37,225 --> 02:01:39,225
They came from Amasya.

1289
02:01:40,745 --> 02:01:42,125
Amasya.

1290
02:01:43,665 --> 02:01:46,425
Then Sheik Nail Effendi must have
sent them.

1291
02:01:47,245 --> 02:01:49,305
It is the tradition.

1292
02:01:49,305 --> 02:01:52,945
Sheik's send each other whatever grows
in their lands.

1293
02:01:54,005 --> 02:01:56,585
Many people love Sheik Edebalı.

1294
02:01:57,145 --> 02:01:59,725
Many Sheiks sent gifts from all kinds of
lands.

1295
02:02:00,025 --> 02:02:02,025
My Sheik is the light of Oghuz!

1296
02:02:25,885 --> 02:02:27,605
Did you miss me too?

1297
02:02:27,705 --> 02:02:29,085
I missed you.

1298
02:02:36,105 --> 02:02:37,645
My Kayı!

1299
02:02:37,745 --> 02:02:39,745
My son!

1300
02:02:40,865 --> 02:02:43,765
No one will separate us ever again.

1301
02:02:45,605 --> 02:02:48,785
I will always keep you next to me,
my baby.

1302
02:02:50,285 --> 02:02:54,365
Is there anything more beautiful than
the reunion of a mother and her child?

1303
02:02:57,445 --> 02:02:58,985
Thankfully.

1304
02:03:03,465 --> 02:03:05,615
Who knows how you felt when
you had a child...

1305
02:03:06,105 --> 02:03:08,445
... after all this time, Bala Hatun?

1306
02:03:10,005 --> 02:03:12,055
I am sure what you've been through was
hard.

1307
02:03:16,685 --> 02:03:18,265
It was a trial, Selvi Hatun.

1308
02:03:19,525 --> 02:03:23,105
No one knows or can choose it.

1309
02:03:28,225 --> 02:03:29,605
Aygül!

1310
02:03:30,105 --> 02:03:32,485
You finally reunited with your Kayı!

1311
02:03:33,125 --> 02:03:34,445
Thankfully, mother.

1312
02:03:39,405 --> 02:03:41,605
How can I pay you, mother?

1313
02:03:41,945 --> 02:03:44,025
There is nothing to pay.

1314
02:03:44,445 --> 02:03:46,965
You paid his foster mother.

1315
02:03:47,345 --> 02:03:50,305
From now on, you will be the mother
of your child.

1316
02:03:59,705 --> 02:04:02,085
This is an important day.

1317
02:04:02,685 --> 02:04:04,525
-Peace be with you.
-Peace be with you.

1318
02:04:04,525 --> 02:04:06,525
Thank you.
Thank you.

1319
02:04:07,705 --> 02:04:09,025
Peace be with you.

1320
02:04:09,115 --> 02:04:11,705
-Peace be with you.
-Peace be with you.

1321
02:04:11,795 --> 02:04:13,295
Thank you.

1322
02:04:22,105 --> 02:04:24,135
In the name of Allah!

1323
02:04:24,265 --> 02:04:26,325
In the name of Allah!

1324
02:06:09,285 --> 02:06:10,595
Make way!

1325
02:06:19,185 --> 02:06:21,765
May peace be with you, people of sharia.

1326
02:06:25,065 --> 02:06:27,655
May peace be with you.

1327
02:06:32,935 --> 02:06:35,625
May peace be with you.

1328
02:06:38,425 --> 02:06:41,615
May peace be with you.

1329
02:06:42,945 --> 02:06:44,845
Tell me...

1330
02:06:46,125 --> 02:06:52,585
...who is our journeyman you wish to be
licensed and what is his profession?

1331
02:06:53,545 --> 02:06:56,815
Working on the grass, under the sky.

1332
02:06:57,865 --> 02:07:01,265
Eager to fight on the battlefield.

1333
02:07:01,795 --> 02:07:03,365
Wishes your prayers.

1334
02:07:04,545 --> 02:07:08,735
Shepherd Akça, carpenter journeyman.

1335
02:07:11,665 --> 02:07:13,555
He is in your presence...

1336
02:07:14,415 --> 02:07:16,945
...with the hope of being a master.

1337
02:07:26,985 --> 02:07:28,525
In the name of Allah!

1338
02:09:14,235 --> 02:09:15,615
He is done.

1339
02:09:20,105 --> 02:09:21,815
In the name of Allah!

1340
02:09:21,925 --> 02:09:23,925
In the name of Allah!

1341
02:10:26,775 --> 02:10:28,775
We dressed you on the outside...

1342
02:10:29,335 --> 02:10:32,145
...may Allah fill you on the inside.

1343
02:10:32,725 --> 02:10:34,045
Amen.

1344
02:10:35,535 --> 02:10:40,805
Respect the truth and sharia in your
profession.

1345
02:10:41,665 --> 02:10:46,605
Control your hands and tongue.

1346
02:10:48,815 --> 02:10:52,055
Use your scale straight.

1347
02:11:58,850 --> 02:12:01,880
To turn Söğüt into a dark corridor...

1348
02:12:02,450 --> 02:12:06,850
...the light has divided the darkness
but I will reunite it.

1349
02:12:21,920 --> 02:12:27,750
There will not be a single point in this
land where darkness does not rule.

1350
02:12:28,770 --> 02:12:32,510
Light of Oghuz or Börü of the Sky...

1351
02:12:32,950 --> 02:12:37,040
...no one will be able to stand against
us.

1352
02:12:44,370 --> 02:12:48,720
Drown in the firelight and perish!

1353
02:12:53,140 --> 02:12:55,200
I, the Lord of the Darkness...

1354
02:12:55,790 --> 02:12:57,610
...will hide in the dark.

1355
02:13:01,410 --> 02:13:04,100
Until we destroy you all one by one...

1356
02:13:19,090 --> 02:13:22,860
...until there's no one left.

1357
